et" id="mwOw">]</span></span></a></sup></div></th></tr><tr class="mergedrow"><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>•<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Capital City</th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euro" title="Euro">€</a>279.938 billion</td></tr><tr class="mergedrow"><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>•<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Metro</th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euro" title="Euro">€</a>865.652 billion</td></tr><tr class="mergedtoprow"><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_zone" title="Time zone">Time<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>zone</a></th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UTC+01:00" title="UTC+01:00">UTC+01:00</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_European_Time" title="Central European Time">CET</a>)</td></tr><tr class="mergedrow"><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><span class="nowrap"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>•<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Summer (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daylight_saving_time" title="Daylight saving time">DST</a>)</span></th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UTC+02:00" title="UTC+02:00">UTC+02:00</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_European_Summer_Time" title="Central European Summer Time">CEST</a>)</td></tr><tr class="mergedtoprow"><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/INSEE_code" title="INSEE code">INSEE</a>/Postal code</th><td class="infobox-data adr"><div class="postal-code"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.insee.fr/fr/statistiques/1405599?geo=COM-75056" class="external text">75056</a> /75001–75020, 75116</div></td></tr><tr class="mergedtoprow"><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Elevation</th><td class="infobox-data">28–131<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>m (92–430<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>ft) <br/>(avg. 78<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>m or 256<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>ft)</td></tr><tr class="mergedtoprow"><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Website</th><td class="infobox-data"><span class="official-website"><span class="url"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.paris.fr/" class="external text">www<wbr/>.paris<wbr/>.fr</a></span></span> <span class="mw-valign-text-top" typeof="mw:File/Frameless" data-mw='{"caption":"Edit this at Wikidata"}'><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q90#P856" title="Edit this at Wikidata"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr-progressive.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8a/OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr-progressive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr-progressive.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Edit this at Wikidata" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20" data-file-type="drawing" height="10" width="10" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" class="infobox-below"><sup><b>1</b></sup> French Land Register data, which excludes lakes, ponds, glaciers <span typeof="mw:Entity">></span> 1<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>km<sup>2</sup> (0.386<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>sq<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>mi or 247 acres) and river estuaries.</td></tr></tbody></table>

<p id="mwPA"><b id="mwPQ">Paris</b><sup about="#mwt60" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-8"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{small|English:}} {{IPAc-en|ˈ|p|æ|r|ɪ|s}} {{respell|PARR|iss}};&lt;ref>{{cite web |title=Paris |url=https://www.ldoceonline.com/dictionary/paris |website=Longman Dictionary of Contemporary English Online |access-date=31 October 2025}}&lt;/ref> {{IPA|fr|paʁi|lang|audio=Paris Pronunciation in French by James Tamim.ogg}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-8" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwPg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQA">[</span>b<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQQ">]</span></span></a></sup> is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_city" title="Capital city" id="mwQg">capital</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_communes_in_France_with_over_20,000_inhabitants" title="List of communes in France with over 20,000 inhabitants" id="mwQw">largest city</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/France" title="France" id="mwRA">France</a>, with an estimated city population of 2.04 million in an area of <span about="#mwt74" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwRQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"105.4"},"2":{"wt":"km2"},"3":{"wt":"sqmi"},"abbr":{"wt":"on"}},"i":0}}]}'>105.4</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt74"> </span><span about="#mwt74">km</span><sup about="#mwt74">2</sup><span about="#mwt74"> (40.7</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt74"> </span><span about="#mwt74">sq</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt74"> </span><span about="#mwt74">mi)</span>, <span about="#mwt75" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwRg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"lc":{"wt":"y"},"1":{"wt":"2026"},"2":{"wt":"January"}},"i":0}}]}'>as of January</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt75"> </span><span about="#mwt75">2026</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt75"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Paris&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Paris&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt75"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_January_2026" about="#mwt75"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt75" id="mwRw"/>,<sup about="#mwt76" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Pop.Paris_5-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Pop.Paris"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Pop.Paris-5" id="mwSA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSw">]</span></span></a></sup> and a metropolitan population of 13.3 million (2023). Located on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine" title="Seine" id="mwTA">Seine</a> in the centre of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île-de-France" title="Île-de-France" id="mwTQ">Île-de-France</a> region, it is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_metropolitan_areas_in_Europe" title="List of metropolitan areas in Europe" id="mwTg">largest metropolitan area</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_cities_in_the_European_Union_by_population_within_city_limits" title="List of cities in the European Union by population within city limits" id="mwTw">fourth-most populous city</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Union" title="European Union" id="mwUA">European Union</a> (EU). Paris is nicknamed the "City of Light" mainly due to its leading role in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Age_of_Enlightenment" title="Age of Enlightenment" id="mwUQ">Age of Enlightenment</a>.</p>

<p id="mwUg">Administratively, Paris is divided into <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrondissements_of_Paris" title="Arrondissements of Paris" id="mwUw">twenty arrondissements</a> (districts), each having their own cultural identity. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haussmann's_renovation_of_Paris" title="Haussmann's renovation of Paris" id="mwVA">Haussmann's renovation of Paris</a>, which created new boulevards, parks, and public works, gave birth to a modern city known as the "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris,_Capital_of_the_19th_Century" title="Paris, Capital of the 19th Century" id="mwVQ">capital of the 19th century</a>". Paris is a major railway, motorway, and air-transport hub; in 2024 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_de_Gaulle_Airport" title="Charles de Gaulle Airport" class="mw-redirect" id="mwVg">Charles de Gaulle Airport</a> was the EU's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_the_busiest_airports_in_Europe" title="List of the busiest airports in Europe" id="mwVw">busiest airport</a>. Paris has one of the most <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sustainable_transportation" title="Sustainable transportation" class="mw-redirect" id="mwWA">sustainable transportation</a> systems in the world and is one of only two cities that have received the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sustainable_Transport_Award" title="Sustainable Transport Award" id="mwWQ">Sustainable Transport Award</a> twice. Its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Art_Nouveau" title="Art Nouveau" id="mwWg">Art Nouveau</a>-decorated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Métro" title="Paris Métro" class="mw-redirect" id="mwWw">Métro</a> has become a symbol of the city. Paris is known for its museums and architectural landmarks: the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louvre" title="Louvre" id="mwXA">Louvre</a> is the largest and most-visited museum in the world; the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musée_d'Orsay" title="Musée d'Orsay" id="mwXQ">Musée d'Orsay</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musée_Marmottan_Monet" title="Musée Marmottan Monet" id="mwXg">Musée Marmottan Monet</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musée_de_l'Orangerie" title="Musée de l'Orangerie" id="mwXw">Musée de l'Orangerie</a> are noted for their collections of French <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impressionism" title="Impressionism" id="mwYA">Impressionist</a> art, while the <span title="French-language text" about="#mwt77" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwYQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"fr"},"2":{"wt":"[[Musée National d&apos;Art Moderne]]"},"italic":{"wt":"no"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="fr" style="font-style: normal;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musée_National_d'Art_Moderne" title="Musée National d'Art Moderne">Musée National d'Art Moderne</a></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text" about="#mwt77" id="mwYg"/>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musée_Rodin" title="Musée Rodin" id="mwYw">Musée Rodin</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musée_Picasso" title="Musée Picasso" class="mw-redirect" id="mwZA">Musée Picasso</a> are noted for their collections of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modern_art" title="Modern art" id="mwZQ">modern</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contemporary_art" title="Contemporary art" id="mwZg">contemporary art</a>. Parts of the city along the Seine have been designated a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNESCO" title="UNESCO" id="mwZw">UNESCO</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Heritage_Site" title="World Heritage Site" id="mwaA">World Heritage Site</a> <span about="#mwt78" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwaQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"since":{"wt":"y"},"1":{"wt":"1991"},"lc":{"wt":"y"}},"i":0}}]}'>since 1991</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt78"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Paris&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Paris&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt78"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_1991" about="#mwt78"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt78" id="mwag"/>.</p>

<p id="mwaw">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_France" title="President of France" id="mwbA">president of France</a> and both houses of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Parliament" title="French Parliament" id="mwbQ">French Parliament</a> sit in Paris. Paris is home to several <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations" title="United Nations" id="mwbg">United Nations</a> organisations, including UNESCO, as well as other international organisations such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OECD" title="OECD" id="mwbw">OECD</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Bureau_of_Weights_and_Measures" title="International Bureau of Weights and Measures" id="mwcA">International Bureau of Weights and Measures</a> (in neighbouring <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint-Cloud" title="Saint-Cloud" id="mwcQ">Saint-Cloud</a>), the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Energy_Agency" title="International Energy Agency" id="mwcg">International Energy Agency</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organisation_internationale_de_la_Francophonie" title="Organisation internationale de la Francophonie" id="mwcw">Organisation internationale de la Francophonie</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Federation_for_Human_Rights" title="International Federation for Human Rights" id="mwdA">International Federation for Human Rights</a>, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fédération_Internationale_de_l'Automobile" title="Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile" id="mwdQ">Fédération internationale de l'Automobile</a>, along with European bodies such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Space_Agency" title="European Space Agency" id="mwdg">European Space Agency</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Banking_Authority" title="European Banking Authority" id="mwdw">European Banking Authority</a>, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Securities_and_Markets_Authority" title="European Securities and Markets Authority" id="mweA">European Securities and Markets Authority</a>. The city <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sport_in_Paris" title="Sport in Paris" class="mw-redirect" id="mweQ">hosts many sporting events</a>, such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Open" title="French Open" id="mweg">French Open</a>, and is the home of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Association_football" title="Association football" id="mwew">association football</a> club <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Saint-Germain_FC" title="Paris Saint-Germain FC" id="mwfA">Paris Saint-Germain</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rugby_union" title="Rugby union" id="mwfQ">rugby union</a> club <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stade_Français" title="Stade Français" id="mwfg">Stade Français</a>. Paris has also hosted the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer_Olympics" title="Summer Olympics" class="mw-redirect" id="mwfw">Summer Olympics</a> three times, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1900_Summer_Olympics" title="1900 Summer Olympics" id="mwgA">1900</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1924_Summer_Olympics" title="1924 Summer Olympics" id="mwgQ">1924</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_Summer_Olympics" title="2024 Summer Olympics" id="mwgg">2024</a>.</p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwgw" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwhA" aria-labelledby="Etymology"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Etymology">Etymology</h2></div>
<p id="mwhQ">The ancient <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oppidum" title="Oppidum" id="mwhg">oppidum</a> that corresponds to the modern city of Paris was first mentioned in the mid-1st century BC by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Caesar" title="Julius Caesar" id="mwhw">Julius Caesar</a> as <i id="mwiA">Lutetia Parisiorum</i> ('<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lutetia" title="Lutetia" id="mwiQ">Lutetia</a> of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parisii_(France)" title="Parisii (France)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwig">Parisii</a>') and is later attested as <i id="mwiw">Parision</i> in the 5th century AD, then as <i id="mwjA">Paris</i> in 1265.<sup about="#mwt79" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTENègre1990155_9-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTENègre1990155"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENègre1990155-9"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Nègre"},"2":{"wt":"1990"},"p":{"wt":"155"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTENègre1990155-9" id="mwjQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwjg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjw">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt89" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Falileyev_10-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Falileyev"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Falileyev-10" id="mwkQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwkg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkw">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlA">]</span></span></a></sup> During the Roman period, it was commonly known as <span title="Latin-language text" about="#mwt82" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwlQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"la"},"2":{"wt":"Lutetia"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="la">Lutetia</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Latin-language_text" about="#mwt82" id="mwlg"/> in Latin, which is interpreted as either stemming from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celtic_languages" title="Celtic languages" id="mwlw">Celtic</a> root <i id="mwmA">*lukot-</i> ('mouse'), or from *<i id="mwmQ">luto-</i> ('marsh, swamp').<sup about="#mwt83" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTELambert199438_11-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTELambert199438"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELambert199438-11"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lambert"},"2":{"wt":"1994"},"p":{"wt":"38"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTELambert199438-11" id="mwmg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwmw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnA">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt86" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003211_12-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003211"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003211-12"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Delamarre"},"2":{"wt":"2003"},"p":{"wt":"211"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003211-12" id="mwng"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwnw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwoA">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwoQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt90" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Falileyev_10-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Falileyev"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Falileyev-10" id="mwog"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpA">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwpg">The name <i id="mwpw">Paris</i> is derived from its early inhabitants, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parisii_(France)" title="Parisii (France)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwqA">Parisii</a>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gauls" title="Gauls" id="mwqQ">Gallic</a> tribe from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Tène_culture" title="La Tène culture" id="mwqg">Iron Age</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_period" title="Roman period" class="mw-redirect" id="mwqw">Roman period</a>.<sup about="#mwt91" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003247_13-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003247"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003247-13"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Delamarre"},"2":{"wt":"2003"},"p":{"wt":"247"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003247-13" id="mwrA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwrQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrg">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrw">]</span></span></a></sup> The meaning of the Gaulish <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethnonym" title="Ethnonym" id="mwsA">ethnonym</a> remains debated. According to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xavier_Delamarre" title="Xavier Delamarre" id="mwsQ">Xavier Delamarre</a>, it may derive from the Celtic root <i id="mwsg">pario-</i> ('cauldron').<sup about="#mwt94" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003247_13-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003247"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003247-13"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Delamarre"},"2":{"wt":"2003"},"p":{"wt":"247"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDelamarre2003247-13" id="mwsw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtQ">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtg">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfred_Holder" title="Alfred Holder" id="mwtw">Alfred Holder</a> interpreted the name as 'the makers' or 'the commanders', by comparing it to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_language" title="Welsh language" id="mwuA">Welsh</a> <i id="mwuQ">peryff</i> ('lord, commander'), both possibly descending from a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-Celtic" title="Proto-Celtic" class="mw-redirect" id="mwug">Proto-Celtic</a> form reconstructed as *<i id="mwuw">kwar-is-io</i>-.<sup about="#mwt97" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBusse2006199_14-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBusse2006199"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBusse2006199-14"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Busse"},"2":{"wt":"2006"},"p":{"wt":"199"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBusse2006199-14" id="mwvA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvg">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvw">]</span></span></a></sup> Alternatively, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pierre-Yves_Lambert" title="Pierre-Yves Lambert" id="mwwA">Pierre-Yves Lambert</a> proposed to translate <i id="mwwQ">Parisii</i> as the 'spear people', by connecting the first element to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Irish" title="Old Irish" id="mwwg">Old Irish</a> <i id="mwww">carr</i> ('spear'), derived from an earlier *<i id="mwxA">kwar-sā</i>.<sup about="#mwt101" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Falileyev_10-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Falileyev"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Falileyev-10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Falileyev-10" id="mwxQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwxg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxw">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwyQ">Residents of the city are known in English as Parisians and in French as <i id="mwyg">Parisiens</i> (<span class="IPA nowrap" lang="fr-Latn-fonipa" about="#mwt102" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwyw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"IPA","href":"./Template:IPA"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"fr"},"2":{"wt":"paʁizjɛ̃"},"3":{"wt":""},"4":{"wt":"Parisien2.ogg"}},"i":0}}]}'><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/French" title="Help:IPA/French"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>paʁizjɛ̃<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></span><span about="#mwt102"> </span><span class="ext-phonos" typeof="mw:Extension/phonos" about="#mwt102" data-mw='{"name":"phonos","attrs":{"file":"Parisien2.ogg"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'><span data-nosnippet="" id="ooui-php-2" class="noexcerpt ext-phonos-PhonosButton ext-phonos-PhonosButton-emptylabel oo-ui-widget oo-ui-widget-enabled oo-ui-buttonElement oo-ui-buttonElement-frameless oo-ui-buttonElement-size-medium oo-ui-iconElement oo-ui-buttonWidget" data-ooui='{"_":"mw.Phonos.PhonosButton","href":"\/\/upload.wikimedia.org\/wikipedia\/commons\/transcoded\/c\/cb\/Parisien2.ogg\/Parisien2.ogg.mp3","rel":["nofollow"],"framed":false,"icon":"volumeUp","data":{"ipa":"","text":"","lang":"en","wikibase":"","file":"Parisien2.ogg"},"classes":["noexcerpt","ext-phonos-PhonosButton","ext-phonos-PhonosButton-emptylabel"]}'><a role="button" tabindex="0" href="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/cb/Parisien2.ogg/Parisien2.ogg.mp3" rel="nofollow" aria-label="Play audio" title="Play audio" class="oo-ui-buttonElement-button"><span class="oo-ui-iconElement-icon oo-ui-icon-volumeUp"></span><span class="oo-ui-labelElement-label"></span><span class="oo-ui-indicatorElement-indicator oo-ui-indicatorElement-noIndicator"></span></a></span><sup class="ext-phonos-attribution noexcerpt navigation-not-searchable"><a href="/wiki/File:Parisien2.ogg" title="File:Parisien2.ogg">ⓘ</a></sup></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Pages_with_French_IPA" about="#mwt102"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Pages_including_recorded_pronunciations" about="#mwt102" id="mwzA"/>). They are also pejoratively called <i id="mwzQ">Parigots</i> (<span class="IPA nowrap" lang="fr-Latn-fonipa" about="#mwt104" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwzg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"IPA","href":"./Template:IPA"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"fr"},"2":{"wt":"paʁiɡo"},"3":{"wt":""},"4":{"wt":"Parigot.ogg"}},"i":0}}]}'><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/French" title="Help:IPA/French"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>paʁiɡo<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></span><span about="#mwt104"> </span><span class="ext-phonos" typeof="mw:Extension/phonos" about="#mwt104" data-mw='{"name":"phonos","attrs":{"file":"Parigot.ogg"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'><span data-nosnippet="" id="ooui-php-3" class="noexcerpt ext-phonos-PhonosButton ext-phonos-PhonosButton-emptylabel oo-ui-widget oo-ui-widget-enabled oo-ui-buttonElement oo-ui-buttonElement-frameless oo-ui-buttonElement-size-medium oo-ui-iconElement oo-ui-buttonWidget" data-ooui='{"_":"mw.Phonos.PhonosButton","href":"\/\/upload.wikimedia.org\/wikipedia\/commons\/transcoded\/b\/b9\/Parigot.ogg\/Parigot.ogg.mp3","rel":["nofollow"],"framed":false,"icon":"volumeUp","data":{"ipa":"","text":"","lang":"en","wikibase":"","file":"Parigot.ogg"},"classes":["noexcerpt","ext-phonos-PhonosButton","ext-phonos-PhonosButton-emptylabel"]}'><a role="button" tabindex="0" href="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b9/Parigot.ogg/Parigot.ogg.mp3" rel="nofollow" aria-label="Play audio" title="Play audio" class="oo-ui-buttonElement-button"><span class="oo-ui-iconElement-icon oo-ui-icon-volumeUp"></span><span class="oo-ui-labelElement-label"></span><span class="oo-ui-indicatorElement-indicator oo-ui-indicatorElement-noIndicator"></span></a></span><sup class="ext-phonos-attribution noexcerpt navigation-not-searchable"><a href="/wiki/File:Parigot.ogg" title="File:Parigot.ogg">ⓘ</a></sup></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Pages_with_French_IPA" about="#mwt104"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Pages_including_recorded_pronunciations" about="#mwt104" id="mwzw"/>).<sup about="#mwt106" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDottin2018535_15-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDottin2018535"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDottin2018535-15"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Dottin"},"2":{"wt":"2018"},"p":{"wt":"535"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDottin2018535-15" id="mw0A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw0Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0g">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0w">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mw1A" aria-labelledby="History"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="History">History</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt109" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw1Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"History of Paris"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt110" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt109" id="mw1g">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Paris" title="History of Paris">History of Paris</a></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt111" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw1w" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"For timeline","href":"./Template:For_timeline"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt112" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt111" id="mw2A">For a chronological guide, see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_Paris" title="Timeline of Paris">Timeline of Paris</a>.</div>

<section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mw2Q" aria-labelledby="Origins"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Origins">Origins</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt113" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw2g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lutetia"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt114" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt113" id="mw2w">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lutetia" title="Lutetia">Lutetia</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mw3A"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ParisiiCoins.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mw3Q"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ParisiiCoins.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/ParisiiCoins.jpg/250px-ParisiiCoins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/ParisiiCoins.jpg/500px-ParisiiCoins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1028" data-file-height="528" data-file-type="bitmap" height="128" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mw3g"/></a><figcaption id="mw3w">Gold coins minted by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parisii_(Gaul)" title="Parisii (Gaul)" id="mw4A">Parisii</a>, 1st century BC</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mw4Q">The <i id="mw4g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parisii_(Gaul)" title="Parisii (Gaul)" id="mw4w">Parisii</a></i> people inhabited the Paris area from around the middle of the 3rd century BC.<sup about="#mwt115" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTECunliffe2004201_16-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTECunliffe2004201"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECunliffe2004201-16"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Cunliffe"},"2":{"wt":"2004"},"p":{"wt":"201"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTECunliffe2004201-16" id="mw5A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw5Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5g">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5w">]</span></span></a></sup> One of the area's major north–south trade routes crossed the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine" title="Seine" id="mw6A">Seine</a> on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île_de_la_Cité" title="Île de la Cité" id="mw6Q">Île de la Cité</a>, which gradually became an important trading centre.<sup about="#mwt118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201025_17-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201025-17"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lawrence"},"2":{"wt":"Gondrand"},"3":{"wt":"2010"},"p":{"wt":"25"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201025-17" id="mw6g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw6w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7A">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7Q">]</span></span></a></sup> The Parisii traded with many river towns, some as far away as the Iberian Peninsula, and minted their own coins.<sup about="#mwt121" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidt200965–70_18-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESchmidt200965–70"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidt200965–70-18"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Schmidt"},"2":{"wt":"2009"},"pp":{"wt":"65–70"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidt200965–70-18" id="mw7g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw7w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8A">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw8g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Caesar" title="Julius Caesar" id="mw8w">Julius Caesar</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gallic_Wars" title="Gallic Wars" id="mw9A">conquered</a> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Basin" title="Paris Basin" id="mw9Q">Paris Basin</a> for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Republic" title="Roman Republic" id="mw9g">Roman Republic</a> in 52 BC and began the Roman settlement on Paris's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rive_Gauche" title="Rive Gauche" id="mw9w">Left Bank</a>.<sup about="#mwt124" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidt200988–104_19-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESchmidt200988–104"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidt200988–104-19"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Schmidt"},"2":{"wt":"2009"},"pp":{"wt":"88–104"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidt200988–104-19" id="mw-A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw-Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-g">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-w">]</span></span></a></sup> The Roman town was originally called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lutetia" title="Lutetia" id="mw_A">Lutetia</a>, more fully, <i id="mw_Q">Lutetia Parisiorum</i>, "Lutetia of the Parisii", modern French <i id="mw_g">Lutèce</i>. It became a prosperous city with a forum, baths, temples, theatres, and an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphitheatre" title="Amphitheatre" id="mw_w">amphitheatre</a>.<sup about="#mwt127" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidt2009154–167_20-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESchmidt2009154–167"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidt2009154–167-20"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Schmidt"},"2":{"wt":"2009"},"pp":{"wt":"154–167"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidt2009154–167-20" id="mwAQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQI">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAQQ">By the end of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Roman_Empire" title="Western Roman Empire" id="mwAQU">Western Roman Empire</a>, the town was known as <i id="mwAQY">Parisius</i>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latin_language" title="Latin language" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAQc">Latin</a> name that later became <i id="mwAQg">Paris</i> in French.<sup about="#mwt130" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMeunier201412_21-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEMeunier201412"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMeunier201412-21"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Meunier"},"2":{"wt":"2014"},"p":{"wt":"12"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMeunier201412-21" id="mwAQk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQs">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQw">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christianity" title="Christianity" id="mwAQ0">Christianity</a> was introduced in the middle of the 3rd century AD by Saint <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Denis_of_Paris" title="Saint Denis of Paris" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAQ4">Denis</a>, the first Bishop of Paris: according to legend, when he refused to renounce his faith before the Roman occupiers, he was beheaded on the hill which became known as <i id="mwAQ8">Mons Martyrum</i> (Latin "Hill of Martyrs"), later "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montmartre" title="Montmartre" id="mwARA">Montmartre</a>", from where he walked headless to the north of the city; the place where he fell and was buried became an important religious shrine, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basilica_of_Saint-Denis" title="Basilica of Saint-Denis" id="mwARE">Basilica of Saint-Denis</a>, and many French kings are buried there.<sup about="#mwt133" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidt2009210–211_22-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESchmidt2009210–211"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidt2009210–211-22"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Schmidt"},"2":{"wt":"2009"},"pp":{"wt":"210–211"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidt2009210–211-22" id="mwARI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARQ">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwARY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:FranceEnglandCard2_052.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwARc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:FranceEnglandCard2_052.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/FranceEnglandCard2_052.jpg/250px-FranceEnglandCard2_052.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/FranceEnglandCard2_052.jpg/500px-FranceEnglandCard2_052.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1600" data-file-height="1200" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwARg"/></a><figcaption id="mwARk">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wall_of_Philip_II_Augustus" title="Wall of Philip II Augustus" id="mwARo">Wall of Philippe Auguste</a>, oldest city wall in Paris</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwARs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clovis_I" title="Clovis I" id="mwARw">Clovis the Frank</a>, the first king of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merovingian_dynasty" title="Merovingian dynasty" id="mwAR0">Merovingian dynasty</a>, made the city his capital from 508.<sup about="#mwt142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-23" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-23"}}'><a href="#cite_note-23" id="mwAR4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAR8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASA">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASE">]</span></span></a></sup> As the Frankish domination of Gaul began, there was a gradual immigration by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franks" title="Franks" id="mwASI">Franks</a> to Paris, and the Parisian <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francien_language" title="Francien language" id="mwASM">Francien</a> dialects were born. Fortification of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île_de_la_Cité" title="Île de la Cité" id="mwASQ">Île de la Cité</a> failed to avert <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Paris_(845)" title="Siege of Paris (845)" id="mwASU">sacking by Vikings in 845</a>. Still, Paris's strategic importance—with its bridges preventing ships from passing—was established by successful defence in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Paris_(885–886)" title="Siege of Paris (885–886)" id="mwASY">Siege of Paris (885–886)</a>, for which the then <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Count_of_Paris" title="Count of Paris" id="mwASc">Count of Paris</a> (<i id="mwASg">comte de Paris</i>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odo_of_France" title="Odo of France" id="mwASk">Odo of France</a>, was elected king of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Francia" title="West Francia" id="mwASo">West Francia</a>.<sup about="#mwt136" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEJones199448_24-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEJones199448"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEJones199448-24"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Jones"},"2":{"wt":"1994"},"p":{"wt":"48"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEJones199448-24" id="mwASs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS0">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS4">]</span></span></a></sup> From the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Capet" title="House of Capet" id="mwAS8">Capetian</a> dynasty that began with the 987 election of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_Capet" title="Hugh Capet" id="mwATA">Hugh Capet</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Count_of_Paris" title="Count of Paris" id="mwATE">Count of Paris</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duke_of_the_Franks" title="Duke of the Franks" id="mwATI">Duke of the Franks</a> (<i id="mwATM">duc des Francs</i>), as king of a unified <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Francia" title="West Francia" id="mwATQ">West Francia</a>, Paris gradually became the largest and most prosperous city in France.<sup about="#mwt139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidt2009210–211_22-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESchmidt2009210–211"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidt2009210–211-22"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Schmidt"},"2":{"wt":"2009"},"pp":{"wt":"210–211"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidt2009210–211-22" id="mwATU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATc">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwATk" aria-labelledby="High_and_Late_Middle_Ages_to_Louis_XIV"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="High_and_Late_Middle_Ages_to_Louis_XIV">High and Late Middle Ages to Louis XIV</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt143" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwATo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Paris in the Middle Ages"},"2":{"wt":"Paris in the 16th century"},"3":{"wt":"Paris in the 17th century"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt144" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt143" id="mwATs">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_in_the_Middle_Ages" title="Paris in the Middle Ages">Paris in the Middle Ages</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_in_the_16th_century" title="Paris in the 16th century">Paris in the 16th century</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_in_the_17th_century" title="Paris in the 17th century">Paris in the 17th century</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwATw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Palais_de_la_Cite.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAT0"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Palais_de_la_Cite.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Palais_de_la_Cite.jpg/250px-Palais_de_la_Cite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Palais_de_la_Cite.jpg/500px-Palais_de_la_Cite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="The Palais de la Cité and Sainte-Chapelle, viewed from the Left Bank, from the Très Riches Heures du duc de Berry (month of June) (1410)" data-file-width="1127" data-file-height="757" data-file-type="bitmap" height="168" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAT4"/></a><figcaption id="mwAT8">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palais_de_la_Cité" title="Palais de la Cité" id="mwAUA">Palais de la Cité</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sainte-Chapelle" title="Sainte-Chapelle" id="mwAUE">Sainte-Chapelle</a>, viewed from the Left Bank, from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Très_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry" title="Très Riches Heures du duc de Berry" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAUI">Très Riches Heures du duc de Berry</a>, June 1410</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwAUM">By the end of the 12th century, Paris had become the political, economic, religious, and cultural capital of France.<sup about="#mwt145" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201027_25-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201027"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201027-25"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lawrence"},"2":{"wt":"Gondrand"},"3":{"wt":"2010"},"p":{"wt":"27"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201027-25" id="mwAUQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUY">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUc">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maurice_de_Sully" title="Maurice de Sully" id="mwAUg">Maurice de Sully</a>, bishop of Paris, started the construction of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notre_Dame_de_Paris" title="Notre Dame de Paris" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAUk">Notre Dame Cathedral</a> in 1163, and was completed after 182 years.<sup about="#mwt157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-26" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-26"}}'><a href="#cite_note-26" id="mwAUo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUw">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAU0">]</span></span></a></sup> After the marshland between the river Seine and <span class="cleanup-needed-content" style="padding-left:0.1em; padding-right:0.1em; color:var(--color-subtle, #54595d); border:1px solid var(--border-color-subtle, #c8ccd1);" about="#mwt148" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAU4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"clarify","href":"./Template:Clarify"},"params":{"text":{"wt":"its slower &apos;dead arm&apos; to its north was filled in"},"date":{"wt":"August 2025"},"reason":{"wt":"the phrase describes the physical evolution of Paris, referring specifically to an ancient, slower-side channel (\"a dead arm\") of the Seine River that once existed just north of the historical core."}},"i":0}}]}'>its slower 'dead arm' to its north was filled in</span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Wikipedia_articles_needing_clarification_from_August_2025" about="#mwt148"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template " style="margin-left:0.1em; white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt148" id="mwAU8"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Please_clarify" title="Wikipedia:Please clarify"><span title='the phrase describes the physical evolution of Paris, referring specifically to an ancient, slower-side channel ("a dead arm") of the Seine River that once existed just north of the historical core. (August 2025)'>clarification needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup> from around the 10th century,<sup about="#mwt149" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBussmann198522_27-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBussmann198522"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBussmann198522-27"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Bussmann"},"2":{"wt":"1985"},"p":{"wt":"22"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBussmann198522-27" id="mwAVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVI">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVM">]</span></span></a></sup> Paris's cultural centre began to move to the Right Bank. In 1137, a new city marketplace (today's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Halles" title="Les Halles" id="mwAVQ">Les Halles</a>) replaced the two smaller ones on the Île de la Cité and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Place_de_l'Hôtel-de-Ville_–_Esplanade_de_la_Libération" title="Place de l'Hôtel-de-Ville – Esplanade de la Libération" id="mwAVU">Place de Grève (Place de l'Hôtel de Ville)</a>.<sup about="#mwt152" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEde_VitriacoHinnebusch1972262_28-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEde VitriacoHinnebusch1972262"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEde_VitriacoHinnebusch1972262-28"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"de Vitriaco"},"2":{"wt":"Hinnebusch"},"3":{"wt":"1972"},"p":{"wt":"262"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEde_VitriacoHinnebusch1972262-28" id="mwAVY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVg">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVk">]</span></span></a></sup> The latter location housed the headquarters of Paris's river trade corporation. This organisation later became, unofficially (although formally in later years), Paris's first municipal government.</p>

<p id="mwAVo">In the late 12th century, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_II_of_France" title="Philip II of France" id="mwAVs">Philip Augustus</a> extended the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louvre" title="Louvre" id="mwAVw">Louvre</a> fortress to defend the city against river invasions from the west, gave the city its first walls between 1190 and 1215, rebuilt its bridges to either side of its central island, and paved its main thoroughfares.<sup about="#mwt158" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant201236–40_29-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant201236–40"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant201236–40-29"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"pp":{"wt":"36–40"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant201236–40-29" id="mwAV0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAV4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAV8">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWA">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1190, he transformed Paris's former cathedral school into a student-teacher corporation that became the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Paris" title="University of Paris" id="mwAWE">University of Paris</a> and drew students from all of Europe.<sup about="#mwt161" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant201228–29_30-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant201228–29"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant201228–29-30"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"pp":{"wt":"28–29"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant201228–29-30" id="mwAWI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWQ">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt164" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201027_25-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201027"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201027-25"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lawrence"},"2":{"wt":"Gondrand"},"3":{"wt":"2010"},"p":{"wt":"27"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201027-25" id="mwAWY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWg">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAWo">With 200,000 inhabitants in 1328, Paris, then already the capital of France, was the most populous city of Europe. By comparison, London in 1300 had 80,000 inhabitants.<sup about="#mwt170" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ParisDigest_31-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ParisDigest"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ParisDigest-31"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ParisDigest-31" id="mwAWs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW0">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW4">]</span></span></a></sup> Around 1340 the city had between 250,000 and 300,000 inhabitants.<sup about="#mwt173" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-32" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-32"}}'><a href="#cite_note-32" id="mwAW8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXE">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXI">]</span></span></a></sup> By the early fourteenth century, so much filth had collected inside urban Europe that French and Italian cities were naming streets after human waste. In medieval Paris, several street names were inspired by <span title="French-language text" about="#mwt167" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAXM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"fr"},"2":{"wt":"merde"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="fr">merde</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text" about="#mwt167" id="mwAXQ"/>, the French word for "shit".<sup about="#mwt174" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-33" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-33"}}'><a href="#cite_note-33" id="mwAXU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXc">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAXk"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P1030887_Paris_IV_hôtel_de_Sens_rwk.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAXo"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P1030887_Paris_IV_hôtel_de_Sens_rwk.JPG" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/P1030887_Paris_IV_h%C3%B4tel_de_Sens_rwk.JPG/250px-P1030887_Paris_IV_h%C3%B4tel_de_Sens_rwk.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/P1030887_Paris_IV_h%C3%B4tel_de_Sens_rwk.JPG/500px-P1030887_Paris_IV_h%C3%B4tel_de_Sens_rwk.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="1488" data-file-height="1412" data-file-type="bitmap" height="237" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAXs"/></a><figcaption id="mwAXw">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hôtel_de_Sens" title="Hôtel de Sens" id="mwAX0">Hôtel de Sens</a> (<abbr title="circa" about="#mwt175" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAX4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Circa","href":"./Template:Circa"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>c.</abbr> 15th–16th), former residence of the Archbishop of Sens</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAX8">During the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hundred_Years'_War" title="Hundred Years' War" id="mwAYA">Hundred Years' War</a>, Paris was occupied by England-friendly <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgundian_State" title="Burgundian State" id="mwAYE">Burgundian forces</a> from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_coup_d'état_and_massacres_of_1418" title="Paris coup d'état and massacres of 1418" id="mwAYI">1418</a>, before being occupied outright by the English when <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_V_of_England" title="Henry V of England" id="mwAYM">Henry V of England</a> entered the French capital in 1420;<sup about="#mwt179" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-34" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-34"}}'><a href="#cite_note-34" id="mwAYQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYY">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYc">]</span></span></a></sup> despite a 1429 effort by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joan_of_Arc" title="Joan of Arc" id="mwAYg">Joan of Arc</a> to liberate the city,<sup about="#mwt176" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro199652–53_35-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro199652–53"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro199652–53-35"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"pages":{"wt":"52–53"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro199652–53-35" id="mwAYk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYs">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYw">]</span></span></a></sup> it would remain under English occupation until 1436.</p>

<p id="mwAY0">In the late 16th century <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Wars_of_Religion" title="French Wars of Religion" id="mwAY4">French Wars of Religion</a>, Paris was a stronghold of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catholic_League_(French)" title="Catholic League (French)" id="mwAY8">Catholic League</a>, the organisers of 24 August 1572 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Bartholomew's_Day_massacre" title="St. Bartholomew's Day massacre" id="mwAZA">St. Bartholomew's Day massacre</a> in which thousands of French Protestants were killed.<sup about="#mwt188" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-36" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-36"}}'><a href="#cite_note-36" id="mwAZE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZM">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt180" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBayrou1994121–130_37-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBayrou1994121–130"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBayrou1994121–130-37"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Bayrou"},"2":{"wt":"1994"},"pp":{"wt":"121–130"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBayrou1994121–130-37" id="mwAZU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZc">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZg">]</span></span></a></sup> The conflicts ended when pretender to the throne <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_IV_of_France" title="Henry IV of France" id="mwAZk">Henry IV</a>, after converting to Catholicism to gain entry to the capital, entered the city in 1594 to claim the crown of France. This king made several improvements to the capital during his reign: he completed the construction of Paris's first uncovered, sidewalk-lined bridge, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pont_Neuf" title="Pont Neuf" id="mwAZo">Pont Neuf</a>, built a Louvre extension connecting it to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuileries_Palace" title="Tuileries Palace" id="mwAZs">Tuileries Palace</a>, and created the first Paris residential square, the Place Royale, now <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Place_des_Vosges" title="Place des Vosges" id="mwAZw">Place des Vosges</a>. Despite Henry IV's efforts to improve city circulation, the narrowness of Paris's streets was a contributing factor in his assassination near <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Halles" title="Les Halles" id="mwAZ0">Les Halles</a> marketplace in 1610.<sup about="#mwt183" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996577_38-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996577"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996577-38"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"577"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996577-38" id="mwAZ4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZ8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaA">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAaI">During the 17th century, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardinal_Richelieu" title="Cardinal Richelieu" id="mwAaM">Cardinal Richelieu</a>, chief minister of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_XIII" title="Louis XIII" id="mwAaQ">Louis XIII</a>, was determined to make Paris the most beautiful city in Europe. He built five new bridges, a new chapel for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/College_of_Sorbonne" title="College of Sorbonne" id="mwAaU">College of Sorbonne</a>, and a palace for himself, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palais-Royal" title="Palais-Royal" id="mwAaY">Palais-Cardinal</a>. After Richelieu died in 1642, it was renamed the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palais-Royal" title="Palais-Royal" id="mwAac">Palais-Royal</a>.<sup about="#mwt189" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996582_39-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996582"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996582-39"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"582"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996582-39" id="mwAag"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAak"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAao">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAas">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAaw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Plan_de_Paris_en_1657.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAa0"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Plan_de_Paris_en_1657.JPG" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Plan_de_Paris_en_1657.JPG/250px-Plan_de_Paris_en_1657.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Plan_de_Paris_en_1657.JPG/500px-Plan_de_Paris_en_1657.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="5500" data-file-height="4605" data-file-type="bitmap" height="209" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAa4"/></a><figcaption id="mwAa8">Lutetia Parisiorum vulgo Paris, Plan de Paris en 1657, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_Janssonius" title="Jan Janssonius" id="mwAbA">Jan Janssonius</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAbE">Due to the Parisian uprisings during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fronde" title="Fronde" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAbI">Fronde</a> civil war, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_XIV" title="Louis XIV" id="mwAbM">Louis XIV</a> moved his court to a new palace, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palace_of_Versailles" title="Palace of Versailles" id="mwAbQ">Versailles</a>, in 1682. Although no longer the capital of France, arts and sciences in the city flourished with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comédie-Française" title="Comédie-Française" id="mwAbU">Comédie-Française</a>, the Academy of Painting, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Academy_of_Sciences" title="French Academy of Sciences" id="mwAbY">French Academy of Sciences</a>. To demonstrate that the city was safe from attack, the king had the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_walls_of_Paris" title="City walls of Paris" id="mwAbc">city walls</a> demolished and replaced with tree-lined boulevards that would become the <i id="mwAbg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boulevards_of_Paris#The_grands_boulevards" title="Boulevards of Paris" id="mwAbk">Grands Boulevards</a></i>.<sup about="#mwt192" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTECombeau200342–43_40-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTECombeau200342–43"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECombeau200342–43-40"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Combeau"},"2":{"wt":"2003"},"pp":{"wt":"42–43"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTECombeau200342–43-40" id="mwAbo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbw">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAb0">]</span></span></a></sup> Other marks of his reign were the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collège_des_Quatre-Nations" title="Collège des Quatre-Nations" id="mwAb4">Collège des Quatre-Nations</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Place_Vendôme" title="Place Vendôme" id="mwAb8">Place Vendôme</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Place_des_Victoires" title="Place des Victoires" id="mwAcA">Place des Victoires</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Invalides" title="Les Invalides" id="mwAcE">Les Invalides</a>.<sup about="#mwt195" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996590–591_41-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996590–591"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996590–591-41"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"pp":{"wt":"590–591"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996590–591-41" id="mwAcI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcQ">[</span>39<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAcY">Paris has been one of the world's major centres of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finance" title="Finance" id="mwAcc">finance</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomacy" title="Diplomacy" id="mwAcg">diplomacy</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commerce" title="Commerce" id="mwAck">commerce</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Culture" title="Culture" id="mwAco">culture</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fashion_capital" title="Fashion capital" id="mwAcs">fashion</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gastronomy" title="Gastronomy" id="mwAcw">gastronomy</a> since the 17th century.<sup about="#mwt200" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-42" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-42"}}'><a href="#cite_note-42" id="mwAc0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAc4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc8">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwAdE" aria-labelledby="18th_and_19th_centuries"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="18th_and_19th_centuries">18th and 19th centuries</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt201" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAdI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Paris in the 18th century"},"2":{"wt":"Paris during the Second Empire"},"3":{"wt":"Haussmann&apos;s renovation of Paris"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt202" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt201" id="mwAdM">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_in_the_18th_century" title="Paris in the 18th century">Paris in the 18th century</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_during_the_Second_Empire" title="Paris during the Second Empire">Paris during the Second Empire</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haussmann's_renovation_of_Paris" title="Haussmann's renovation of Paris">Haussmann's renovation of Paris</a></div>
<p id="mwAdQ">Paris grew in population from about 400,000 in 1640 to 650,000 in 1780.<sup about="#mwt214" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-43" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-43"}}'><a href="#cite_note-43" id="mwAdU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdc">[</span>41<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdg">]</span></span></a></sup> A new boulevard named the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champs-Élysées" title="Champs-Élysées" id="mwAdk">Champs-Élysées</a> extended the city west to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Place_Charles_de_Gaulle" title="Place Charles de Gaulle" id="mwAdo">Étoile</a>,<sup about="#mwt203" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTECombeau200345–47_44-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTECombeau200345–47"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECombeau200345–47-44"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Combeau"},"2":{"wt":"2003"},"pp":{"wt":"45–47"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTECombeau200345–47-44" id="mwAds"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd0">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd4">]</span></span></a></sup> while the working-class neighbourhood of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faubourg_Saint-Antoine" title="Faubourg Saint-Antoine" id="mwAd8">Faubourg Saint-Antoine</a> on the eastern side of the city grew increasingly crowded with poor migrant workers from other regions of France.<sup about="#mwt206" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012129–133_45-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012129–133"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012129–133-45"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"pp":{"wt":"129–133"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012129–133-45" id="mwAeA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeI">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeM">]</span></span></a></sup> Paris's role in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Education_in_France" title="Education in France" id="mwAeQ">education</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_and_technology_in_France" title="Science and technology in France" id="mwAeU">sciences</a> led Paris to be known as the City of Light during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Age_of_Enlightenment" title="Age of Enlightenment" id="mwAeY">age of Enlightenment</a> in the 18th century.<sup about="#mwt217" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-46" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-46"}}'><a href="#cite_note-46" id="mwAec"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAek">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt209" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-47" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-47"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{langx|fr|la Ville Lumière}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-47" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwAes"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAew"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAe0">[</span>c<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAe4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAe8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Prise_de_la_Bastille.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAfA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Prise_de_la_Bastille.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Prise_de_la_Bastille.jpg/250px-Prise_de_la_Bastille.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Prise_de_la_Bastille.jpg/500px-Prise_de_la_Bastille.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="8133" data-file-height="6181" data-file-type="bitmap" height="190" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAfE"/></a><figcaption id="mwAfI">The storming of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bastille" title="Bastille" id="mwAfM">Bastille</a> on 14 July 1789, by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean-Pierre_Houël" title="Jean-Pierre Houël" id="mwAfQ">Jean-Pierre Houël</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAfU">In the summer of 1789, Paris became the centre stage of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Revolution" title="French Revolution" id="mwAfY">French Revolution</a>. On 14<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAfc"> </span>July, a mob seized the arsenal at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Invalides" title="Les Invalides" id="mwAfg">Invalides</a>, acquiring thousands of guns, with which it <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Storming_of_the_Bastille" title="Storming of the Bastille" id="mwAfk">stormed the Bastille</a>, a principal symbol of royal authority. The first independent <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Commune_(1789–1795)" title="Paris Commune (1789–1795)" id="mwAfo">Paris Commune</a>, or city council, met in the <i id="mwAfs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hôtel_de_Ville,_Paris" title="Hôtel de Ville, Paris" id="mwAfw">Hôtel de Ville</a></i> and elected a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayor_(France)" title="Mayor (France)" id="mwAf0">Mayor</a>, the astronomer <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_Sylvain_Bailly" title="Jean Sylvain Bailly" id="mwAf4">Jean Sylvain Bailly</a>, on 15<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAf8"> </span>July.<sup about="#mwt218" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPaine1998453_48-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEPaine1998453"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPaine1998453-48"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Paine"},"2":{"wt":"1998"},"p":{"wt":"453"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPaine1998453-48" id="mwAgA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgI">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAgQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_XVI" title="Louis XVI" id="mwAgU">Louis XVI</a> and the royal family were <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women's_march_on_Versailles" title="Women's march on Versailles" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAgY">brought to Paris</a> and incarcerated in the Tuileries Palace. In 1793, as the revolution turned increasingly radical, the king, queen, and mayor were beheaded by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guillotine" title="Guillotine" id="mwAgc">guillotine</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reign_of_Terror" title="Reign of Terror" id="mwAgg">Reign of Terror</a>, along with more than 16,000 others throughout France.<sup about="#mwt221" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996674_49-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996674"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996674-49"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"674"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996674-49" id="mwAgk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgs">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgw">]</span></span></a></sup> The property of the aristocracy and the church was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biens_nationaux" title="Biens nationaux" id="mwAg0">nationalised</a>, and the city's churches were closed, sold, or demolished.<sup about="#mwt224" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012144_50-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012144"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012144-50"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"144"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012144-50" id="mwAg4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAg8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhA">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhE">]</span></span></a></sup> A succession of revolutionary factions ruled Paris until <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coup_of_18_Brumaire" title="Coup of 18 Brumaire" id="mwAhI">9<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAhM"> </span>November 1799</a> (<i id="mwAhQ">coup d'état du 18 brumaire</i>), when <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleon_Bonaparte" title="Napoleon Bonaparte" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAhU">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> seized power as First Consul.<sup about="#mwt227" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012147_51-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012147"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012147-51"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"147"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012147-51" id="mwAhY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhg">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAho">The population of Paris had dropped by 100,000 during the Revolution, but after 1799 it surged with 160,000 new residents, reaching 660,000 by 1815.<sup about="#mwt230" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012148_52-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012148"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012148-52"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"148"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012148-52" id="mwAhs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAh0">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAh4">]</span></span></a></sup> Napoleon replaced the elected government of Paris with a prefect who reported directly to him. He began erecting monuments to military glory, including the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arc_de_Triomphe" title="Arc de Triomphe" id="mwAh8">Arc de Triomphe</a>, and improved the neglected infrastructure of the city with new fountains, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canal_de_l'Ourcq" title="Canal de l'Ourcq" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAiA">Canal de l'Ourcq</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Père_Lachaise_Cemetery" title="Père Lachaise Cemetery" id="mwAiE">Père Lachaise Cemetery</a> and the city's first metal bridge, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pont_des_Arts" title="Pont des Arts" id="mwAiI">Pont des Arts</a>. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arc_de_Triomphe" title="Arc de Triomphe" id="mwAiM">Arc de Triomphe</a> was eventually completed in 1836.<sup about="#mwt233" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012148_52-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012148"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012148-52"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"148"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012148-52" id="mwAiQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAiU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiY">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAic">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAig"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Louis-Emile_Durandelle,_The_Eiffel_Tower_-_State_of_the_Construction,_1888.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAik"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Louis-Emile_Durandelle,_The_Eiffel_Tower_-_State_of_the_Construction,_1888.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Louis-Emile_Durandelle%2C_The_Eiffel_Tower_-_State_of_the_Construction%2C_1888.jpg/250px-Louis-Emile_Durandelle%2C_The_Eiffel_Tower_-_State_of_the_Construction%2C_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Louis-Emile_Durandelle%2C_The_Eiffel_Tower_-_State_of_the_Construction%2C_1888.jpg/500px-Louis-Emile_Durandelle%2C_The_Eiffel_Tower_-_State_of_the_Construction%2C_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3277" data-file-height="4169" data-file-type="bitmap" height="318" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAio"/></a><figcaption id="mwAis">The Eiffel Tower, under construction in November 1888, startled Parisians—and the world—with its modernity.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAiw">During the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bourbon_Restoration_in_France" title="Bourbon Restoration in France" id="mwAi0">Restoration</a>, the bridges and squares of Paris were returned to their pre-Revolution names; the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/July_Revolution" title="July Revolution" id="mwAi4">July Revolution</a> in 1830, commemorated by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/July_Column" title="July Column" id="mwAi8">July Column</a> on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Place_de_la_Bastille" title="Place de la Bastille" id="mwAjA">Place de la Bastille</a>, brought to power a constitutional monarch, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Philippe_I" title="Louis Philippe I" id="mwAjE">Louis Philippe I</a>. The first railway line to Paris opened in 1837, beginning a new period of massive migration from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Provinces_of_France" title="Provinces of France" id="mwAjI">provinces</a> to the city.<sup about="#mwt236" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012148_52-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012148"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012148-52"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"148"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012148-52" id="mwAjM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjU">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjY">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1848, Louis-Philippe was overthrown by a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Revolution_of_1848" title="French Revolution of 1848" id="mwAjc">popular uprising</a> in the streets of Paris. His successor, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleon_III" title="Napoleon III" id="mwAjg">Napoleon III</a>, alongside the newly appointed prefect of the Seine, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georges-Eugène_Haussmann" title="Georges-Eugène Haussmann" id="mwAjk">Georges-Eugène Haussmann</a>, launched a huge public works project to build wide new boulevards, a new opera house, a central market, new aqueducts, sewers and parks, including the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bois_de_Boulogne" title="Bois de Boulogne" id="mwAjo">Bois de Boulogne</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bois_de_Vincennes" title="Bois de Vincennes" id="mwAjs">Bois de Vincennes</a>.<sup about="#mwt239" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDe_Moncan20127–35_53-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDe Moncan20127–35"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDe_Moncan20127–35-53"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"De Moncan"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"pp":{"wt":"7–35"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDe_Moncan20127–35-53" id="mwAjw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAj0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAj4">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAj8">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1860, Napoleon III annexed the surrounding towns and created eight new arrondissements, expanding Paris to its current limits.<sup about="#mwt242" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDe_Moncan20127–35_53-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDe Moncan20127–35"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDe_Moncan20127–35-53"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"De Moncan"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"pp":{"wt":"7–35"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDe_Moncan20127–35-53" id="mwAkA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkI">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAkQ">During the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franco-Prussian_War" title="Franco-Prussian War" id="mwAkU">Franco-Prussian War</a> (1870–1871), Paris was besieged by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prussian_Army" title="Prussian Army" id="mwAkY">Prussian Army</a>. Following several months of blockade, hunger, and then bombardment by the Prussians, the city was forced to surrender on 28<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAkc"> </span>January 1871. After seizing power in Paris on 28<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAkg"> </span>March, a revolutionary government known as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Commune" title="Paris Commune" id="mwAkk">Paris Commune</a> held power for two months, before being harshly suppressed by the French army during the "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semaine_sanglante" title="Semaine sanglante" id="mwAko">Bloody Week</a>" at the end of May 1871.<sup about="#mwt245" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTERougerie2014118_54-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTERougerie2014118"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERougerie2014118-54"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Rougerie"},"2":{"wt":"2014"},"p":{"wt":"118"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTERougerie2014118-54" id="mwAks"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk0">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAk8">In the late 19th century, Paris hosted two major international expositions: the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exposition_Universelle_(1889)" title="Exposition Universelle (1889)" id="mwAlA">1889 Universal Exposition</a>, which featured the new Eiffel Tower, was held to mark the centennial of the French Revolution; and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exposition_Universelle_(1900)" title="Exposition Universelle (1900)" id="mwAlE">1900 Universal Exposition</a> gave Paris the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pont_Alexandre_III" title="Pont Alexandre III" id="mwAlI">Pont Alexandre III</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Palais" title="Grand Palais" id="mwAlM">Grand Palais</a>, the <span title="French-language text" about="#mwt248" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAlQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"fr"},"2":{"wt":"[[Petit Palais]]"},"italic":{"wt":"no"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="fr" style="font-style: normal;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petit_Palais" title="Petit Palais">Petit Palais</a></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text" about="#mwt248" id="mwAlU"/> and the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Métro" title="Paris Métro" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAlY">Paris Métro</a> line.<sup about="#mwt249" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFraserSpalding2011117_55-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFraserSpalding2011117"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFraserSpalding2011117-55"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fraser"},"2":{"wt":"Spalding"},"3":{"wt":"2011"},"p":{"wt":"117"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFraserSpalding2011117-55" id="mwAlc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlk">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlo">]</span></span></a></sup> Paris became the laboratory of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naturalism_(literature)" title="Naturalism (literature)" id="mwAls">Naturalism</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Émile_Zola" title="Émile Zola" id="mwAlw">Émile Zola</a>) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symbolism_(arts)" title="Symbolism (arts)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAl0">Symbolism</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Baudelaire" title="Charles Baudelaire" id="mwAl4">Charles Baudelaire</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Verlaine" title="Paul Verlaine" id="mwAl8">Paul Verlaine</a>), and of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impressionism" title="Impressionism" id="mwAmA">Impressionism</a> in art (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Courbet" title="Courbet" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAmE">Courbet</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manet" title="Manet" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAmI">Manet</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_Monet" title="Claude Monet" id="mwAmM">Monet</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renoir" title="Renoir" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAmQ">Renoir</a>).<sup about="#mwt252" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996490–491_56-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996490–491"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996490–491-56"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"pp":{"wt":"490–491"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996490–491-56" id="mwAmU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmc">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwAmk" aria-labelledby="20th_and_21st_centuries"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="20th_and_21st_centuries">20th and 21st centuries</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt255" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAmo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Paris in the Belle Époque"},"2":{"wt":"Paris during the First World War"},"3":{"wt":"Paris between the Wars (1919–1939)"},"4":{"wt":"Paris in World War II"},"5":{"wt":"History of Paris (1946–2000)"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt256" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt255" id="mwAms">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_in_the_Belle_Époque" title="Paris in the Belle Époque">Paris in the Belle Époque</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_during_the_First_World_War" title="Paris during the First World War" class="mw-redirect">Paris during the First World War</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_between_the_Wars_(1919–1939)" title="Paris between the Wars (1919–1939)" class="mw-redirect">Paris between the Wars (1919–1939)</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_in_World_War_II" title="Paris in World War II">Paris in World War II</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Paris_(1946–2000)" title="History of Paris (1946–2000)">History of Paris (1946–2000)</a></div>
<p id="mwAmw">By 1901, the population of Paris had grown to about 2,715,000.<sup about="#mwt257" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTECombeau200361_57-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTECombeau200361"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECombeau200361-57"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Combeau"},"2":{"wt":"2003"},"p":{"wt":"61"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTECombeau200361-57" id="mwAm0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAm4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAm8">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnA">]</span></span></a></sup> At the beginning of the century, artists from around the world, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pablo_Picasso" title="Pablo Picasso" id="mwAnE">Pablo Picasso</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amedeo_Modigliani" title="Amedeo Modigliani" id="mwAnI">Modigliani</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_Matisse" title="Henri Matisse" id="mwAnM">Henri Matisse</a> made Paris their home. It was the birthplace of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fauvism" title="Fauvism" id="mwAnQ">Fauvism</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cubism" title="Cubism" id="mwAnU">Cubism</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_art" title="Abstract art" id="mwAnY">abstract art</a>,<sup about="#mwt260" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996497_58-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996497"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996497-58"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"497"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996497-58" id="mwAnc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAng"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnk">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAno">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt268" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-59" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-59"}}'><a href="#cite_note-59" id="mwAns"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAn0">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAn4">]</span></span></a></sup> and authors such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcel_Proust" title="Marcel Proust" id="mwAn8">Marcel Proust</a> were exploring new approaches to literature.<sup about="#mwt263" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996491_60-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996491"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996491-60"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"491"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996491-60" id="mwAoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoI">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAoQ">During the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_World_War" title="First World War" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAoU">First World War</a>, Paris sometimes found itself on the front line; 600 to 1,000 Paris taxis played a small but highly important symbolic role in transporting 6,000 soldiers to the front line at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Battle_of_the_Marne" title="First Battle of the Marne" id="mwAoY">First Battle of the Marne</a>. The city was also bombed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zeppelin" title="Zeppelin" id="mwAoc">Zeppelins</a> and shelled by German <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Gun" title="Paris Gun" id="mwAog">long-range guns</a>.<sup about="#mwt269" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996750_61-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996750"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996750-61"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"750"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996750-61" id="mwAok"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAos">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAow">]</span></span></a></sup> In the years after the war, known as <i id="mwAo0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_between_the_Wars_(1919–1939)" title="Paris between the Wars (1919–1939)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAo4">Les Années Folles</a></i>, Paris continued to be a mecca for writers, musicians and artists from around the world, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ernest_Hemingway" title="Ernest Hemingway" id="mwAo8">Ernest Hemingway</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Igor_Stravinsky" title="Igor Stravinsky" id="mwApA">Igor Stravinsky</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Joyce" title="James Joyce" id="mwApE">James Joyce</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josephine_Baker" title="Josephine Baker" id="mwApI">Josephine Baker</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eva_Kotchever" title="Eva Kotchever" id="mwApM">Eva Kotchever</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Miller" title="Henry Miller" id="mwApQ">Henry Miller</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anaïs_Nin" title="Anaïs Nin" id="mwApU">Anaïs Nin</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sidney_Bechet" title="Sidney Bechet" id="mwApY">Sidney Bechet</a><sup about="#mwt272" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEShack2001_62-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEShack2001"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEShack2001-62"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Shack"},"2":{"wt":"2001"},"3":{"wt":""}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEShack2001-62" id="mwApc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApk">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApo">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salvador_Dalí" title="Salvador Dalí" id="mwAps">Salvador Dalí</a>.<sup about="#mwt277" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Meisler_63-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Meisler"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Meisler-63"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Meisler-63" id="mwApw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAp0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp4">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAqA">In the years after the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Peace_Conference,_1919" title="Paris Peace Conference, 1919" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAqE">peace conference</a>, the city was also home to growing numbers of students and activists from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_colonial_empire" title="French colonial empire" id="mwAqI">French colonies</a> and other Asian and African countries, who later became leaders of their countries, such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ho_Chi_Minh" title="Ho Chi Minh" id="mwAqM">Ho Chi Minh</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhou_Enlai" title="Zhou Enlai" id="mwAqQ">Zhou Enlai</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Léopold_Sédar_Senghor" title="Léopold Sédar Senghor" id="mwAqU">Léopold Sédar Senghor</a>.<sup about="#mwt279" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-64" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-64"}}'><a href="#cite_note-64" id="mwAqY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqg">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAqo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:The_Liberation_of_Paris,_25_-_26_August_1944_HU66477.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAqs"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:The_Liberation_of_Paris,_25_-_26_August_1944_HU66477.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/The_Liberation_of_Paris%2C_25_-_26_August_1944_HU66477.jpg/250px-The_Liberation_of_Paris%2C_25_-_26_August_1944_HU66477.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/The_Liberation_of_Paris%2C_25_-_26_August_1944_HU66477.jpg/500px-The_Liberation_of_Paris%2C_25_-_26_August_1944_HU66477.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2480" data-file-height="1819" data-file-type="bitmap" height="183" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAqw"/></a><figcaption id="mwAq0">General <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_de_Gaulle" title="Charles de Gaulle" id="mwAq4">Charles de Gaulle</a> on the Champs-Élysées celebrating the liberation of Paris, 26 August 1944</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAq8">On 14 June 1940, the German army marched into Paris, which had been declared an "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open_city" title="Open city" id="mwArA">open city</a>".<sup about="#mwt280" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012217_65-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012217"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012217-65"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"217"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012217-65" id="mwArE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArM">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArQ">]</span></span></a></sup> On 16–17 July 1942, following German orders, the French police and gendarmes arrested 12,884 Jews, including 4,115 children, and confined them during five days at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vel'_d'Hiv_Roundup" title="Vel' d'Hiv Roundup" class="mw-redirect" id="mwArU"><i id="mwArY">Vel d'Hiv</i></a>, from which they were transported by train to the extermination camp at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auschwitz_concentration_camp" title="Auschwitz concentration camp" id="mwArc">Auschwitz</a>. None of the children came back.<sup about="#mwt283" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996637_66-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996637"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996637-66"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"637"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996637-66" id="mwArg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAro">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt286" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012218_67-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012218"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012218-67"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"218"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012218-67" id="mwArw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAr0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAr4">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAr8">]</span></span></a></sup> On 25 August 1944, the city was liberated by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2nd_Armored_Division_(France)" title="2nd Armored Division (France)" id="mwAsA">French 2nd Armoured Division</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4th_Infantry_Division_(United_States)" title="4th Infantry Division (United States)" id="mwAsE">4th Infantry Division</a> of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Army" title="United States Army" id="mwAsI">United States Army</a>. General <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_de_Gaulle" title="Charles de Gaulle" id="mwAsM">Charles de Gaulle</a> led a huge and emotional crowd down the Champs Élysées towards Notre Dame de Paris and made a rousing speech from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hôtel_de_Ville,_Paris" title="Hôtel de Ville, Paris" id="mwAsQ">Hôtel de Ville</a>.<sup about="#mwt289" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996242–243_68-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996242–243"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996242–243-68"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"pp":{"wt":"242–243"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996242–243-68" id="mwAsU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsc">[</span>65<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAsk">Paris became involved in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algerian_War" title="Algerian War" id="mwAso">Algerian War</a> for independence, which occurred in the 1950s and 1960s; in August 1961, the pro-independence <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Liberation_Front_(Algeria)" title="National Liberation Front (Algeria)" id="mwAss">FLN</a>, targeted and killed 11 Paris policemen, leading to the imposition of a curfew on Muslims of Algeria (who, at that time, were French citizens). On 17 October 1961, an unauthorised but peaceful protest demonstration of Algerians against the curfew led to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1961_Paris_massacre" title="1961 Paris massacre" id="mwAsw">violent confrontations</a> between the police and demonstrators, in which at least 40 people were killed. The anti-independence <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organisation_armée_secrète" title="Organisation armée secrète" id="mwAs0">Organisation armée secrète</a> (OAS) carried out a series of bombings in Paris throughout 1961 and 1962.<sup about="#mwt297" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-69" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-69"}}'><a href="#cite_note-69" id="mwAs4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAs8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtA">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt292" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996658_70-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996658"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996658-70"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"658"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996658-70" id="mwAtI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtQ">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAtY">In May 1968, protesting students occupied the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sorbonne_(building)" title="Sorbonne (building)" id="mwAtc">Sorbonne</a> and put up barricades in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latin_Quarter,_Paris" title="Latin Quarter, Paris" id="mwAtg">Latin Quarter</a>. Thousands of Parisian blue-collar workers joined the students, and the movement grew into a two-week general strike. Supporters of the government won the June elections by a large majority. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/May_1968_events_in_France" title="May 1968 events in France" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAtk">May 1968 events in France</a> resulted in the break-up of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Paris" title="University of Paris" id="mwAto">University of Paris</a> into 13 independent campuses.<sup about="#mwt298" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012226_71-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012226"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012226-71"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"226"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012226-71" id="mwAts"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAt0">[</span>68<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAt4">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1975, the National Assembly changed the status of Paris to that of other French cities and, on 25 March 1977, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacques_Chirac" title="Jacques Chirac" id="mwAt8">Jacques Chirac</a> became the first elected mayor of Paris since 1793.<sup about="#mwt301" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996260_72-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996260"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996260-72"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"260"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996260-72" id="mwAuA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuI">[</span>69<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuM">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwAuQ">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tour_Montparnasse" title="Tour Montparnasse" id="mwAuU">Tour Maine-Montparnasse</a>, the tallest building in the city at 57 storeys and <span about="#mwt304" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAuY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"210"},"2":{"wt":"m"},"3":{"wt":"ft"},"4":{"wt":"0"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"}},"i":0}}]}'>210</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt304"> </span><span about="#mwt304">m (689</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt304"> </span><span about="#mwt304">ft)</span> high, was built between 1969 and 1973. It was highly controversial, and it remains the only building in the centre of the city over 32 storeys high.<sup about="#mwt305" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012222_73-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012222"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012222-73"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"222"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012222-73" id="mwAuc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAug"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuk">[</span>70<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuo">]</span></span></a></sup> The population of Paris dropped from 2,850,000 in 1954 to 2,152,000 in 1990, as middle-class families moved to the suburbs.<sup about="#mwt308" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTECombeau2003107–108_74-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTECombeau2003107–108"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECombeau2003107–108-74"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Combeau"},"2":{"wt":"2003"},"pp":{"wt":"107–108"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTECombeau2003107–108-74" id="mwAus"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAu0">[</span>71<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAu4">]</span></span></a></sup> A suburban railway network, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Réseau_Express_Régional" title="Réseau Express Régional" id="mwAu8">RER</a> (Réseau Express Régional), was built to complement the Métro; the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Périphérique_(Paris)" title="Périphérique (Paris)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAvA">Périphérique</a> expressway encircling the city was completed in 1973.<sup about="#mwt311" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBellde-Shalit2011247_75-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBellde-Shalit2011247"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBellde-Shalit2011247-75"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Bell"},"2":{"wt":"de-Shalit"},"3":{"wt":"2011"},"p":{"wt":"247"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBellde-Shalit2011247-75" id="mwAvE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvM">[</span>72<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The bank of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine" title="Seine" id="mwAvU">Seine</a> in the city centre, which includes the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louvre" title="Louvre" id="mwAvY">Louvre</a> and the Eiffel Tower was classified as a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNESCO_World_Heritage_Site" title="UNESCO World Heritage Site" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAvc">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 1991.<sup about="#mwt316" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-unesco_76-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"unesco"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-unesco-76"}}'><a href="#cite_note-unesco-76" id="mwAvg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvo">[</span>73<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAvw">Most of the postwar presidents of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Fifth_Republic" title="French Fifth Republic" id="mwAv0">Fifth Republic</a> wanted to leave their own monuments in Paris; President <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georges_Pompidou" title="Georges Pompidou" id="mwAv4">Georges Pompidou</a> started the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centre_Georges_Pompidou" title="Centre Georges Pompidou" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAv8">Centre Georges Pompidou</a> (1977), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valéry_Giscard_d'Estaing" title="Valéry Giscard d'Estaing" id="mwAwA">Valéry Giscard d'Estaing</a> began the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musée_d'Orsay" title="Musée d'Orsay" id="mwAwE">Musée d'Orsay</a> (1986); President <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/François_Mitterrand" title="François Mitterrand" id="mwAwI">François Mitterrand</a> had the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opéra_Bastille" title="Opéra Bastille" id="mwAwM">Opéra Bastille</a> built (1985–1989), the new site of the <i id="mwAwQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bibliothèque_nationale_de_France" title="Bibliothèque nationale de France" id="mwAwU">Bibliothèque nationale de France</a></i> (1996), the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arche_de_la_Défense" title="Arche de la Défense" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAwY">Arche de la Défense</a> (1985–1989) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Défense" title="La Défense" id="mwAwc">La Défense</a>, as well as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louvre_Pyramid" title="Louvre Pyramid" id="mwAwg">Louvre Pyramid</a> with its underground courtyard (1983–1989); <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacques_Chirac" title="Jacques Chirac" id="mwAwk">Jacques Chirac</a> (2006), the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musée_du_Quai_Branly_–_Jacques_Chirac" title="Musée du Quai Branly – Jacques Chirac" id="mwAwo">Musée du quai Branly</a>.<sup about="#mwt317" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESarmant2012226–230_77-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESarmant2012226–230"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012226–230-77"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sarmant"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"pp":{"wt":"226–230"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESarmant2012226–230-77" id="mwAws"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAww"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAw0">[</span>74<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAw4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAw8">In the early 21st century, the population of Paris began to increase slowly again, as more young people moved into the city. It reached 2.25 million in 2011. In March 2001, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bertrand_Delanoë" title="Bertrand Delanoë" id="mwAxA">Bertrand Delanoë</a> became the first socialist mayor; he was re-elected in March 2008.<sup about="#mwt322" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-78" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-78"}}'><a href="#cite_note-78" id="mwAxE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxM">[</span>75<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Bertrand Delanoë also transformed a section of the highway along the Left Bank of the Seine into an urban promenade and park, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Promenade_des_Berges_de_la_Seine" title="Promenade des Berges de la Seine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAxU">Promenade des Berges de la Seine</a>, which he inaugurated in June 2013.<sup about="#mwt325" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-79" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-79"}}'><a href="#cite_note-79" id="mwAxY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxg">[</span>76<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAxo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Marche_hommage_Charlie_hebdo_et_aux_victimes_des_attentats_de_janvier_2015_(17).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAxs"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Marche_hommage_Charlie_hebdo_et_aux_victimes_des_attentats_de_janvier_2015_(17).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Marche_hommage_Charlie_hebdo_et_aux_victimes_des_attentats_de_janvier_2015_%2817%29.jpg/250px-Marche_hommage_Charlie_hebdo_et_aux_victimes_des_attentats_de_janvier_2015_%2817%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Marche_hommage_Charlie_hebdo_et_aux_victimes_des_attentats_de_janvier_2015_%2817%29.jpg/500px-Marche_hommage_Charlie_hebdo_et_aux_victimes_des_attentats_de_janvier_2015_%2817%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4256" data-file-height="2832" data-file-type="bitmap" height="166" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAxw"/></a><figcaption id="mwAx0">Demonstrators at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Place_de_la_République" title="Place de la République" id="mwAx4">Place de la République</a>, Paris, 11 January 2015, during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_marches" title="Republican marches" id="mwAx8">Republican marches</a> after the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_Hebdo_shooting" title="Charlie Hebdo shooting" id="mwAyA"><i id="mwAyE">Charlie Hebdo</i> shooting</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAyI">In 2007, President <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Sarkozy" title="Nicolas Sarkozy" id="mwAyM">Nicolas Sarkozy</a> launched the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Paris" title="Grand Paris" id="mwAyQ">Grand Paris</a> project to integrate Paris more closely with the towns in the region around it. After many modifications, the new area, named the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Paris" title="Grand Paris" id="mwAyU">Metropolis of Grand Paris</a>, with a population of 6.7 million, was created on 1 January 2016.<sup about="#mwt330" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Lichfield_80-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Lichfield"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Lichfield-80"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Lichfield-80" id="mwAyY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyg">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyk">]</span></span></a></sup> The City of Paris and the national government approved the plans for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Paris_Express" title="Grand Paris Express" id="mwAyo">Grand Paris Express</a> four years later, totalling <span about="#mwt326" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAys" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"205"},"2":{"wt":"km"},"3":{"wt":"mi"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"}},"i":0}}]}'>205</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt326"> </span><span about="#mwt326">km (127</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt326"> </span><span about="#mwt326">mi)</span> of automated metro lines to connect Paris, the innermost three departments around Paris, airports and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TGV" title="TGV" id="mwAyw">high-speed rail (TGV)</a> stations, at an estimated cost of €35 billion.<sup about="#mwt333" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-metro_81-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"metro"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-metro-81"}}'><a href="#cite_note-metro-81" id="mwAy0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAy4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAy8">[</span>78<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzA">]</span></span></a></sup> The system is scheduled to be completed by 2030.<sup about="#mwt336" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-82" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-82"}}'><a href="#cite_note-82" id="mwAzE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzM">[</span>79<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt327" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAzU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"update after","href":"./Template:Update_after"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2030"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Wikipedia_articles_scheduled_for_update_tagging"/></span>

<p id="mwAzY">A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_2015_Île-de-France_attacks" title="January 2015 Île-de-France attacks" id="mwAzc">series of attacks</a> occurred in the Paris region, especially in Paris, in January 2015, the most serious being the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_Hebdo_shooting" title="Charlie Hebdo shooting" id="mwAzg">shooting at the offices</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_Hebdo" title="Charlie Hebdo" id="mwAzk">Charlie Hebdo</a>. 17 people died in the attacks, which <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Qaeda_in_the_Arabian_Peninsula" title="Al-Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula" id="mwAzo">Al-Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula</a> claimed responsibility.<sup about="#mwt339" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-83" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-83"}}'><a href="#cite_note-83" id="mwAzs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAz0">[</span>80<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAz4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt342" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-84" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-84"}}'><a href="#cite_note-84" id="mwAz8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA0A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0E">[</span>81<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0I">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_marches" title="Republican marches" id="mwA0M">1.5 million people marched in Paris</a> in a show of solidarity against terrorism and in support of freedom of speech.<sup about="#mwt345" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-85" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-85"}}'><a href="#cite_note-85" id="mwA0Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA0U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0Y">[</span>82<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0c">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/November_2015_Paris_attacks" title="November 2015 Paris attacks" id="mwA0g">Terrorist attacks</a>, claimed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islamic_State" title="Islamic State" id="mwA0k">ISIL</a>,<sup about="#mwt348" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-86" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-86"}}'><a href="#cite_note-86" id="mwA0o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA0s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0w">[</span>83<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA00">]</span></span></a></sup> occurred again in November, which killed 130 people and injured more than 350.<sup about="#mwt351" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-87" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-87"}}'><a href="#cite_note-87" id="mwA04"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA08"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1A">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1E">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwA1I">In an aim to limit the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Effects_of_climate_change" title="Effects of climate change" id="mwA1M">effects of climate change</a> below 2<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwA1Q"> </span>°C, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Agreement" title="Paris Agreement" id="mwA1U">Paris Agreement</a> was signed by 196 nations of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Framework_Convention_on_Climate_Change" title="United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change" id="mwA1Y">United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change</a> on 22 April 2016 in Paris.<sup about="#mwt354" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-88" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-88"}}'><a href="#cite_note-88" id="mwA1c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA1g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1k">[</span>85<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1o">]</span></span></a></sup> The following year, billionaire <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/François_Pinault" title="François Pinault" id="mwA1s">François Pinault</a> received a 50‑year lease to convert the historic <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bourse_de_commerce_(Paris)" title="Bourse de commerce (Paris)" id="mwA1w">Bourse de Commerce</a> into a contemporary art museum, overseen by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_people" title="Japanese people" id="mwA10">Japanese</a> architect <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tadao_Ando" title="Tadao Ando" id="mwA14">Tadao Ando</a>.<sup about="#mwt357" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-89" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-89"}}'><a href="#cite_note-89" id="mwA18"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA2A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2E">[</span>86<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2I">]</span></span></a></sup> Construction was delayed by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic" title="COVID-19 pandemic" id="mwA2M">COVID-19 pandemic</a>, reopening in May 2021.<sup about="#mwt360" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-90" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-90"}}'><a href="#cite_note-90" id="mwA2Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA2U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2Y">[</span>87<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2c">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notre-Dame_fire" title="Notre-Dame fire" id="mwA2g">Notre Dame Cathedral caught fire</a> on 15 April 2019, beginning in the eaves of its roof,<sup about="#mwt363" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Notre-Dame_91-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Notre-Dame"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Notre-Dame-91"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Notre-Dame-91" id="mwA2k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA2o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2s">[</span>88<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2w">]</span></span></a></sup> engulfing the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spire" title="Spire" id="mwA20">spire</a> and most of the roof. Firefighters were able to control the blaze, saving the main structure including the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell_tower" title="Bell tower" id="mwA24">bell towers</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_window" title="Rose window" id="mwA28">rose windows</a>, and there were no injuries;<sup about="#mwt364" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Notre-Dame_91-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Notre-Dame"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Notre-Dame-91" id="mwA3A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3I">[</span>88<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3M">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reopening_of_Notre-Dame_de_Paris" title="Reopening of Notre-Dame de Paris" id="mwA3Q">it was reopened</a> on 7 December 2024.<sup about="#mwt367" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-92" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-92"}}'><a href="#cite_note-92" id="mwA3U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3c">[</span>89<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwA3k">In terms of international connectedness, as of 2024, Paris was one of eight cities worldwide that was classified as an "Alpha+" city by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Globalization_and_World_Cities_Research_Network" title="Globalization and World Cities Research Network" id="mwA3o">Globalization and World Cities Research Network</a>.<sup about="#mwt371" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-93" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-93"}}'><a href="#cite_note-93" id="mwA3s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA30">[</span>90<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA34">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_that_may_have_off-topic_sections" about="#mwt368" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA38" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"relevance inline","href":"./Template:Relevance_inline"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"August 2025"},"reason":{"wt":"What does that mean to the reader? Doesn&apos;t sound very important."}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Wikipedia_articles_that_may_have_off-topic_sections_from_August_2025" about="#mwt368"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template " style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt368" id="mwA4A"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Writing_better_articles#Stay_on_topic" title="Wikipedia:Writing better articles"><span title="The material near this tag may contain information that is not relevant to the article's main topic. What does that mean to the reader? Doesn't sound very important. (August 2025)">relevant?</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwA4E" aria-labelledby="Geography"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Geography">Geography</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt372" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA4I" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Geography of Paris"},"2":{"wt":"Climate of Paris"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt373" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt372" id="mwA4M">Main articles: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geography_of_Paris" title="Geography of Paris">Geography of Paris</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_of_Paris" title="Climate of Paris">Climate of Paris</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwA4Q"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris,_France_ESA24382977.jpeg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwA4U"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris,_France_ESA24382977.jpeg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Paris%2C_France_ESA24382977.jpeg/250px-Paris%2C_France_ESA24382977.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Paris%2C_France_ESA24382977.jpeg/500px-Paris%2C_France_ESA24382977.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="6023" data-file-height="4015" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwA4Y"/></a><figcaption id="mwA4c">A 2022 satellite image of Paris, by ESA's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sentinel-2" title="Sentinel-2" id="mwA4g">Sentinel-2</a> mission</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwA4k">Paris is located in northern central France, in a north-bending arc of the river <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine" title="Seine" id="mwA4o">Seine</a>, whose crest includes two islands, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île_Saint-Louis" title="Île Saint-Louis" id="mwA4s">Île Saint-Louis</a> and the larger <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île_de_la_Cité" title="Île de la Cité" id="mwA4w">Île de la Cité</a>, which form the oldest part of Paris. The river's mouth on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Channel" title="English Channel" id="mwA40">English Channel</a> (<i id="mwA44">La Manche</i>) is about <span about="#mwt374" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA48" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"233"},"2":{"wt":"mi"}},"i":0}}]}'>233</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt374"> </span><span about="#mwt374">mi (375</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt374"> </span><span about="#mwt374">km)</span> downstream from Paris. Paris is spread widely on both banks of the river.<sup about="#mwt382" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-City_94-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"City"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-City-94"}}'><a href="#cite_note-City-94" id="mwA5A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5I">[</span>91<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5M">]</span></span></a></sup> Overall, Paris is relatively flat, and the lowest point is <span about="#mwt375" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA5Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"35"},"2":{"wt":"m"}},"i":0}}]}'>35</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt375"> </span><span about="#mwt375">m (115</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt375"> </span><span about="#mwt375">ft)</span> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Above_mean_sea_level" title="Above mean sea level" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA5U">above sea level</a>. Paris has several prominent hills, the highest of which is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montmartre" title="Montmartre" id="mwA5Y">Montmartre</a> at <span about="#mwt376" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA5c" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"130"},"2":{"wt":"m"},"3":{"wt":"ft"},"4":{"wt":"0"}},"i":0}}]}'>130</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt376"> </span><span about="#mwt376">m (427</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt376"> </span><span about="#mwt376">ft)</span>.<sup about="#mwt377" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBlackmoreMcConnachie2004153_95-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBlackmoreMcConnachie2004153"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBlackmoreMcConnachie2004153-95"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Blackmore"},"2":{"wt":"McConnachie"},"3":{"wt":"2004"},"p":{"wt":"153"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBlackmoreMcConnachie2004153-95" id="mwA5g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5o">[</span>92<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5s">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwA5w">Excluding the outlying parks of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bois_de_Boulogne" title="Bois de Boulogne" id="mwA50">Bois de Boulogne</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bois_de_Vincennes" title="Bois de Vincennes" id="mwA54">Bois de Vincennes</a>, Paris covers an oval measuring about <span about="#mwt383" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA58" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"87"},"2":{"wt":"km2"}},"i":0}}]}'>87</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt383"> </span><span about="#mwt383">km</span><sup about="#mwt383">2</sup><span about="#mwt383"> (34</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt383"> </span><span about="#mwt383">sq</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt383"> </span><span about="#mwt383">mi)</span> in area, enclosed by the <span about="#mwt384" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA6A" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"35"},"2":{"wt":"km"},"adj":{"wt":"on"}},"i":0}}]}'>35</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt384"> </span><span about="#mwt384">km (22</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt384"> </span><span about="#mwt384">mi)</span> ring road, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boulevard_Périphérique" title="Boulevard Périphérique" id="mwA6E">Boulevard Périphérique</a>.<sup about="#mwt385" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201069_96-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201069"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201069-96"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lawrence"},"2":{"wt":"Gondrand"},"3":{"wt":"2010"},"p":{"wt":"69"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand201069-96" id="mwA6I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6Q">[</span>93<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6U">]</span></span></a></sup> Paris's last major annexation of outlying territories in 1860 gave it its modern form, and created the 20 clockwise-spiralling arrondissements (municipal boroughs). From the 1860 area of <span about="#mwt388" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA6Y" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"78"},"2":{"wt":"km2"}},"i":0}}]}'>78</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt388"> </span><span about="#mwt388">km</span><sup about="#mwt388">2</sup><span about="#mwt388"> (30</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt388"> </span><span about="#mwt388">sq</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt388"> </span><span about="#mwt388">mi)</span>, the city limits were expanded marginally to <span about="#mwt389" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA6c" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"86.9"},"2":{"wt":"km2"}},"i":0}}]}'>86.9</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt389"> </span><span about="#mwt389">km</span><sup about="#mwt389">2</sup><span about="#mwt389"> (33.6</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt389"> </span><span about="#mwt389">sq</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt389"> </span><span about="#mwt389">mi)</span> in the 1920s. In 1929, the Bois de Boulogne and Bois de Vincennes forest parks were annexed to the city, bringing its area to about <span about="#mwt390" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA6g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"105"},"2":{"wt":"km2"}},"i":0}}]}'>105</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt390"> </span><span about="#mwt390">km</span><sup about="#mwt390">2</sup><span about="#mwt390"> (41</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt390"> </span><span about="#mwt390">sq</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt390"> </span><span about="#mwt390">mi)</span>.<sup about="#mwt394" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-97" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-97"}}'><a href="#cite_note-97" id="mwA6k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6s">[</span>94<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6w">]</span></span></a></sup> The metropolitan area is <span about="#mwt391" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA60" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2300"},"2":{"wt":"km2"}},"i":0}}]}'>2,300</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt391"> </span><span about="#mwt391">km</span><sup about="#mwt391">2</sup><span about="#mwt391"> (890</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt391"> </span><span about="#mwt391">sq</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt391"> </span><span about="#mwt391">mi)</span>.<sup about="#mwt395" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-City_94-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"City"}}'><a href="#cite_note-City-94" id="mwA64"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA68"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7A">[</span>91<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7E">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwA7I" aria-labelledby="Climate"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Climate">Climate</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwA7M"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_raining_autumn_cityscape_(8252181936).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwA7Q"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_raining_autumn_cityscape_(8252181936).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Paris_raining_autumn_cityscape_%288252181936%29.jpg/250px-Paris_raining_autumn_cityscape_%288252181936%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Paris_raining_autumn_cityscape_%288252181936%29.jpg/500px-Paris_raining_autumn_cityscape_%288252181936%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="5616" data-file-height="3744" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwA7U"/></a><figcaption id="mwA7Y">Autumn in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avenue_Raphaël?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Avenue Raphaël (page does not exist)" about="#mwt396" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:LocalizedAttrs" class="new" id="mwA7c" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"interlanguage link","href":"./Template:Interlanguage_link"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Avenue Raphaël"},"2":{"wt":"fr"}},"i":0}}]}' data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Avenue Raphaël"]}}'>Avenue Raphaël</a><span class="noprint" style="font-size:85%; font-style: normal; " about="#mwt396" id="mwA7g"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avenue%20Raphaël" title="fr:Avenue Raphaël" class="extiw">fr</a><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></span>, Paris</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwA7k">Paris has a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oceanic_climate" title="Oceanic climate" id="mwA7o">Oceanic climate</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Köppen_climate_classification" title="Köppen climate classification" id="mwA7s">Köppen</a>: <i id="mwA7w">Cfb</i>),<sup about="#mwt409" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-98" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-98"}}'><a href="#cite_note-98" id="mwA70"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA74"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA78">[</span>95<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8A">]</span></span></a></sup> typical of western Europe.<sup about="#mwt412" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-99" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-99"}}'><a href="#cite_note-99" id="mwA8E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8M">[</span>96<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8Q">]</span></span></a></sup> This climate type features cool winters and warm summers, with average temperatures between <span about="#mwt397" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA8U" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"15"},"2":{"wt":"and"},"3":{"wt":"25"},"4":{"wt":"°C"},"5":{"wt":"°F"}},"i":0}}]}'>15 and 25</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt397"> </span><span about="#mwt397">°C (59 and 77</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt397"> </span><span about="#mwt397">°F)</span> in July.<sup about="#mwt398" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand2010309_100-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand2010309"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand2010309-100"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lawrence"},"2":{"wt":"Gondrand"},"3":{"wt":"2010"},"p":{"wt":"309"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTELawrenceGondrand2010309-100" id="mwA8Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8g">[</span>97<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8k">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt415" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-101" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-101"}}'><a href="#cite_note-101" id="mwA8o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8w">[</span>98<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA80">]</span></span></a></sup> Each year there are a few days when the temperature rises above <span about="#mwt401" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA84" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"32"},"2":{"wt":"C"}},"i":0}}]}'>32</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt401"> </span><span about="#mwt401">°C (90</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt401"> </span><span about="#mwt401">°F)</span>. Longer periods of more intense heat sometimes occur, such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2003_European_heat_wave" title="2003 European heat wave" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA88">heat wave of 2003</a>, when temperatures exceeded <span about="#mwt402" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA9A" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"30"},"2":{"wt":"°C"}},"i":0}}]}'>30</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt402"> </span><span about="#mwt402">°C (86</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt402"> </span><span about="#mwt402">°F)</span> for weeks, reached <span about="#mwt403" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA9E" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"40"},"2":{"wt":"°C"}},"i":0}}]}'>40</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt403"> </span><span about="#mwt403">°C (104</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt403"> </span><span about="#mwt403">°F)</span> on some days, and rarely cooled down at night.<sup about="#mwt404" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGoldstein20058_102-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEGoldstein20058"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGoldstein20058-102"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Goldstein"},"2":{"wt":"2005"},"p":{"wt":"8"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGoldstein20058-102" id="mwA9I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA9M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9Q">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9U">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwA9Y">The weather in spring and autumn is generally mild during the day and cool at night, but is unstable.<sup about="#mwt421" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-103" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-103"}}'><a href="#cite_note-103" id="mwA9c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA9g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9k">[</span>100<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9o">]</span></span></a></sup> In winter, sunshine is scarce, days are cool, and nights are cold but generally above freezing, with low temperatures around <span about="#mwt416" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA9s" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"3"},"2":{"wt":"°C"}},"i":0}}]}'>3</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt416"> </span><span about="#mwt416">°C (37</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt416"> </span><span about="#mwt416">°F)</span>.<sup about="#mwt424" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-104" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-104"}}'><a href="#cite_note-104" id="mwA9w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA90"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA94">[</span>101<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA98">]</span></span></a></sup> Light night frosts are quite common, but the temperature seldom dips below <span about="#mwt417" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-A" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"-5"},"2":{"wt":"°C"}},"i":0}}]}'>−5</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt417"> </span><span about="#mwt417">°C (23</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt417"> </span><span about="#mwt417">°F)</span>. Paris sometimes sees light snow or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow_flurry" title="Snow flurry" id="mwA-E">flurries</a> with or without accumulation.<sup about="#mwt427" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-105" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-105"}}'><a href="#cite_note-105" id="mwA-I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA-M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-Q">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-U">]</span></span></a></sup> In summer, the weather is warm, averaging <span about="#mwt418" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-Y" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"22"},"2":{"wt":"°C"}},"i":0}}]}'>22</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt418"> </span><span about="#mwt418">°C (72</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt418"> </span><span about="#mwt418">°F)</span>, and there is 8 hours of sunshine on average per day.<sup about="#mwt430" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-106" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-106"}}'><a href="#cite_note-106" id="mwA-c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA-g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-k">[</span>103<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-o">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwA-s">Paris has an average annual precipitation of <span about="#mwt431" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-w" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"641"},"2":{"wt":"mm"},"3":{"wt":"in"},"4":{"wt":"1"}},"i":0}}]}'>641</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt431"> </span><span about="#mwt431">mm (25.2</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt431"> </span><span about="#mwt431">in)</span>, and experiences light rainfall distributed evenly throughout the year. <span about="#mwt432" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"as of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2025"},"post":{"wt":","}},"i":0}}]}'>As of 2025</span><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt432"></span><span about="#mwt432">,</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt432"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Paris&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Paris&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt432"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2025" about="#mwt432"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt432" id="mwA-4"/> the highest recorded temperature was <span about="#mwt433" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"42.6"},"2":{"wt":"°C"}},"i":0}}]}'>42.6</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt433"> </span><span about="#mwt433">°C (108.7</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt433"> </span><span about="#mwt433">°F)</span>, on 25 July 2019.<sup about="#mwt437" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-107" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-107"}}'><a href="#cite_note-107" id="mwA_A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA_E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_I">[</span>104<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_M">]</span></span></a></sup> The lowest was <span about="#mwt434" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"-23.9"},"2":{"wt":"°C"}},"i":0}}]}'>−23.9</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt434"> </span><span about="#mwt434">°C (−11.0</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt434"> </span><span about="#mwt434">°F)</span>, on 10 December 1879.<sup about="#mwt440" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-climate_108-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"climate"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-climate-108"}}'><a href="#cite_note-climate-108" id="mwA_U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA_Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_c">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<div about="#mwt441" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_k" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Paris weatherbox","href":"./Template:Paris_weatherbox"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>
