</div>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwBAY" aria-labelledby="Administration"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Administration">Administration</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt457" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBAc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Administration of Paris"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt458" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt457" id="mwBAg">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Administration_of_Paris" title="Administration of Paris">Administration of Paris</a></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwBAk" aria-labelledby="City_government"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="City_government">City government</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt459" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBAo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Further","href":"./Template:Further"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Arrondissements of Paris"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt460" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt459" id="mwBAs">Further information: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrondissements_of_Paris" title="Arrondissements of Paris">Arrondissements of Paris</a></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt461" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBAw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":""},"2":{"wt":"Mayor of Paris"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt462" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt461" id="mwBA0">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayor_of_Paris" title="Mayor of Paris">Mayor of Paris</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBA4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_plan_jms.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBA8"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_plan_jms.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Paris_plan_jms.png/250px-Paris_plan_jms.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Paris_plan_jms.png/500px-Paris_plan_jms.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1840" data-file-height="1334" data-file-type="bitmap" height="181" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBBA"/></a><figcaption id="mwBBE">A map of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrondissements_of_Paris" title="Arrondissements of Paris" id="mwBBI">arrondissements of Paris</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwBBM">For almost all of its long history, except for a few brief periods, Paris was governed directly by representatives of the king, emperor, or president of France. In 1974, Paris was granted municipal autonomy by the National Assembly.<sup about="#mwt463" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996334_112-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996334"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996334-112"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"334"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996334-112" id="mwBBQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBBU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBY">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBc">]</span></span></a></sup> The first modern elected mayor of Paris was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacques_Chirac" title="Jacques Chirac" id="mwBBg">Jacques Chirac</a>, elected in March 1977, becoming the city's first mayor since 1871 and only the fourth since 1794. The current mayor is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmanuel_Grégoire" title="Emmanuel Grégoire" id="mwBBk">Emmanuel Grégoire</a>, a member of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socialist_Party_(France)" title="Socialist Party (France)" id="mwBBo">Socialist Party</a>, who was elected in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Paris_municipal_election" title="2026 Paris municipal election" id="mwBBs">2026</a>.<sup about="#mwt468" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-113" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-113"}}'><a href="#cite_note-113" id="mwBBw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBB0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBB4">[</span>110<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBB8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBCA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris,_Hôtel_de_Ville_--_2014_--_1714.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBCE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris,_Hôtel_de_Ville_--_2014_--_1714.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Paris%2C_H%C3%B4tel_de_Ville_--_2014_--_1714.jpg/250px-Paris%2C_H%C3%B4tel_de_Ville_--_2014_--_1714.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Paris%2C_H%C3%B4tel_de_Ville_--_2014_--_1714.jpg/500px-Paris%2C_H%C3%B4tel_de_Ville_--_2014_--_1714.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4300" data-file-height="3423" data-file-type="bitmap" height="199" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBCI"/></a><figcaption id="mwBCM">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hôtel_de_Ville,_Paris" title="Hôtel de Ville, Paris" id="mwBCQ">Hôtel de Ville</a>, or city hall</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwBCU">The mayor of Paris is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indirect_election" title="Indirect election" id="mwBCY">elected indirectly</a> by Paris voters. The voters of each of the city's 20 arrondissements elect members to the <i id="mwBCc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conseil_de_Paris" title="Conseil de Paris" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBCg">Conseil de Paris</a></i> (Council of Paris), which elects the mayor. The council is composed of 163 members. Each arrondissement is allocated many seats, dependent upon its population, from 10 members for each of the least-populated arrondissements to 34 members for the most populated. The council is elected using <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Closed_list" title="Closed list" id="mwBCk">closed list</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proportional_representation" title="Proportional representation" id="mwBCo">proportional representation</a> in a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two-round_system" title="Two-round system" id="mwBCs">two-round system</a>.<sup about="#mwt471" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Election_Code_–_Article_L260_114-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Election Code – Article L260"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Election_Code_–_Article_L260-114"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Election_Code_–_Article_L260-114" id="mwBCw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBC0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBC4">[</span>111<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBC8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBDA">Party lists winning an absolute <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Majority" title="Majority" id="mwBDE">majority</a> in the first round – or at least a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plurality_(voting)" title="Plurality (voting)" id="mwBDI">plurality</a> in the second round – automatically win half the seats of an arrondissement. The remaining half of the seats are distributed proportionally to all lists which win at least 5% of the vote, using the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highest_averages_method" title="Highest averages method" id="mwBDM">highest averages method</a>.<sup about="#mwt472" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Election_Code_–_Article_L260_114-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Election Code – Article L260"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Election_Code_–_Article_L260-114" id="mwBDQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBDU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDY">[</span>111<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDc">]</span></span></a></sup> This ensures that the winning party or coalition always wins a majority of the seats, even if they do not win an absolute majority of the vote.<sup about="#mwt475" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Pariscouncil_115-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Pariscouncil"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pariscouncil-115"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Pariscouncil-115" id="mwBDg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBDk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDo">[</span>112<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBDw">Before the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Paris_municipal_election" title="2020 Paris municipal election" id="mwBD0">2020 Paris municipal election</a>, each of Paris's 20 arrondissements had its own town hall and a directly elected council (<span title="French-language text" about="#mwt476" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBD4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"fr"},"2":{"wt":"[[conseil d&apos;arrondissement]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="fr"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conseil_d'arrondissement" title="Conseil d'arrondissement">conseil d'arrondissement</a></i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text" about="#mwt476" id="mwBD8"/>), which elects an arrondissement mayor.<sup about="#mwt477" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEShales200716_116-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEShales200716"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEShales200716-116"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Shales"},"2":{"wt":"2007"},"p":{"wt":"16"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEShales200716-116" id="mwBEA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBEE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEI">[</span>113<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEM">]</span></span></a></sup> The council of each arrondissement is composed of members of the Conseil de Paris, and members who serve only on the council of the arrondissement. The number of deputy mayors in each arrondissement varies depending on its population. As of 1996, there were 20 arrondissement mayors and 120 deputy mayors.<sup about="#mwt480" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFierro1996334_112-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFierro1996334"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996334-112"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fierro"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"334"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFierro1996334-112" id="mwBEQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBEU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEY">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEc">]</span></span></a></sup> The creation of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Centre" title="Paris Centre" id="mwBEg">Paris Centre</a>, a unified administrative division with a single mayor covering the first four arrondissements, took effect with the said 2020 election. The other 16 arrondissements continue to have their own mayors.<sup about="#mwt485" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-117" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-117"}}'><a href="#cite_note-117" id="mwBEk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBEo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEs">[</span>114<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwBE0" aria-labelledby="Métropole_du_Grand_Paris"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Métropole_du_Grand_Paris"><span id="M.C3.A9tropole_du_Grand_Paris" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Métropole du Grand Paris</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBE4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Établissements_publics_territoriaux_du_Grand_Paris_et_trois_départements.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBE8"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Établissements_publics_territoriaux_du_Grand_Paris_et_trois_départements.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/%C3%89tablissements_publics_territoriaux_du_Grand_Paris_et_trois_d%C3%A9partements.svg/250px-%C3%89tablissements_publics_territoriaux_du_Grand_Paris_et_trois_d%C3%A9partements.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/%C3%89tablissements_publics_territoriaux_du_Grand_Paris_et_trois_d%C3%A9partements.svg/500px-%C3%89tablissements_publics_territoriaux_du_Grand_Paris_et_trois_d%C3%A9partements.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1534" data-file-height="1882" data-file-type="drawing" height="307" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBFA"/></a><figcaption id="mwBFE">A map of the Greater Paris Metropolis and its governing territories</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBFI">In January 2016, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Paris" title="Grand Paris" id="mwBFM">Métropole du Grand Paris</a> came into existence.<sup about="#mwt487" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MGP_118-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"MGP"}}'><a href="#cite_note-MGP-118" id="mwBFQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBFU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFY">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFc">]</span></span></a></sup> It is an administrative structure for co-operation between the City of Paris and its nearest suburbs. It includes the City of Paris, plus the communes of the three departments of the inner suburbs, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hauts-de-Seine" title="Hauts-de-Seine" id="mwBFg">Hauts-de-Seine</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine-Saint-Denis" title="Seine-Saint-Denis" id="mwBFk">Seine-Saint-Denis</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Val-de-Marne" title="Val-de-Marne" id="mwBFo">Val-de-Marne</a>, plus seven communes in the outer suburbs, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argenteuil" title="Argenteuil" id="mwBFs">Argenteuil</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Val_d'Oise" title="Val d'Oise" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBFw">Val d'Oise</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paray-Vieille-Poste" title="Paray-Vieille-Poste" id="mwBF0">Paray-Vieille-Poste</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Essonne" title="Essonne" id="mwBF4">Essonne</a>, which were added to include the major airports of Paris. The Metropole covers <span about="#mwt486" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBF8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"814"},"2":{"wt":"km2"},"3":{"wt":"sqmi"},"4":{"wt":"0"},"abbr":{"wt":"off"}},"i":0}}]}'>814</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt486"> </span><span about="#mwt486">km</span><sup about="#mwt486">2</sup><span about="#mwt486"> (314</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt486"> </span><span about="#mwt486">sq</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt486"> </span><span about="#mwt486">mi)</span>. In 2015, it had a population of 6.945 million people.<sup about="#mwt490" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-119" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-119"}}'><a href="#cite_note-119" id="mwBGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBGE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGI">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt493" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-lemoniteur1_120-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"lemoniteur1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-lemoniteur1-120"}}'><a href="#cite_note-lemoniteur1-120" id="mwBGQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBGU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGY">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBGg">The new structure is administered by a Metropolitan Council of 210 members, not directly elected, but chosen by the councils of the member Communes. By 2020, its basic competencies will include urban planning, housing, and protection of the environment.<sup about="#mwt494" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MGP_118-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"MGP"}}'><a href="#cite_note-MGP-118" id="mwBGk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBGo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGs">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt495" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-lemoniteur1_120-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"lemoniteur1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-lemoniteur1-120" id="mwBG0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBG4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBG8">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHA">]</span></span></a></sup> In January 2016, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Ollier" title="Patrick Ollier" id="mwBHE">Patrick Ollier</a> was elected the first president of the metropolitan council. Though the Metropole has a population of nearly seven million people and accounts for 25 percent of the GDP of France, it has a very small budget: just 65 million Euros, compared with eight billion Euros for the City of Paris.<sup about="#mwt498" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-121" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-121"}}'><a href="#cite_note-121" id="mwBHI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBHM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHQ">[</span>118<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwBHY" aria-labelledby="Regional_government"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Regional_government">Regional government</h3></div>
<p id="mwBHc">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Region" title="Region" id="mwBHg">Region</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île_de_France" title="Île de France" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBHk">Île de France</a>, including Paris and its surrounding communities, is governed by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regional_Council_of_Île-de-France" title="Regional Council of Île-de-France" id="mwBHo">Regional Council</a>, composed of 209 members representing the different communes. In December 2015, a list of candidates of the Union of the Right, a coalition of centrist and right-wing parties, led by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valérie_Pécresse" title="Valérie Pécresse" id="mwBHs">Valérie Pécresse</a>, narrowly won the regional election, defeating a coalition of Socialists and ecologists. The Socialists had governed the region for seventeen years. The regional council has 121 members from the Union of the Right, 66 from the Union of the Left and 22 from the extreme right National Front.<sup about="#mwt501" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-122" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-122"}}'><a href="#cite_note-122" id="mwBHw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBH0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBH4">[</span>119<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBH8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwBIA" aria-labelledby="National_government"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="National_government">National government</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBIE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Secretary_Pompeo_Arrives_to_Meet_with_French_Foreign_Minister_Le_Drian_in_Paris_(50610423656).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBII"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Secretary_Pompeo_Arrives_to_Meet_with_French_Foreign_Minister_Le_Drian_in_Paris_(50610423656).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Secretary_Pompeo_Arrives_to_Meet_with_French_Foreign_Minister_Le_Drian_in_Paris_%2850610423656%29.jpg/250px-Secretary_Pompeo_Arrives_to_Meet_with_French_Foreign_Minister_Le_Drian_in_Paris_%2850610423656%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Secretary_Pompeo_Arrives_to_Meet_with_French_Foreign_Minister_Le_Drian_in_Paris_%2850610423656%29.jpg/500px-Secretary_Pompeo_Arrives_to_Meet_with_French_Foreign_Minister_Le_Drian_in_Paris_%2850610423656%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="9086" data-file-height="6057" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBIM"/></a><figcaption id="mwBIQ">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Élysée_Palace" title="Élysée Palace" id="mwBIU">Élysée Palace</a>, official residence of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_France" title="President of France" id="mwBIY">President of France</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBIc">As the capital of France, Paris is the seat of France's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_France" title="Government of France" id="mwBIg">national government</a>. For the executive, the two chief officers each have their own official residences, which also serve as their offices. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_France" title="President of France" id="mwBIk">President of the French Republic</a> resides at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Élysée_Palace" title="Élysée Palace" id="mwBIo">Élysée Palace</a>.<sup about="#mwt510" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-123" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-123"}}'><a href="#cite_note-123" id="mwBIs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBIw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBI0">[</span>120<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBI4">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_France" title="Prime Minister of France" id="mwBI8">Prime Minister</a>'s seat is at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hôtel_Matignon" title="Hôtel Matignon" id="mwBJA">Hôtel Matignon</a>.<sup about="#mwt513" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-124" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-124"}}'><a href="#cite_note-124" id="mwBJE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBJI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJM">[</span>121<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt502" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKnappWright200693–94_125-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEKnappWright200693–94"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKnappWright200693–94-125"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Knapp"},"2":{"wt":"Wright"},"3":{"wt":"2006"},"pp":{"wt":"93–94"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKnappWright200693–94-125" id="mwBJU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBJY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJc">[</span>122<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJg">]</span></span></a></sup> Government ministries are located in various parts of the city, many near the Hôtel Matignon.<sup about="#mwt505" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBorrus2012288_126-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBorrus2012288"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBorrus2012288-126"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Borrus"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"288"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBorrus2012288-126" id="mwBJk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBJo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJs">[</span>123<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBJ0">Both houses of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Parliament" title="French Parliament" id="mwBJ4">French Parliament</a> are located on the Rive Gauche. The upper house, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senate_(France)" title="Senate (France)" id="mwBJ8">Senate</a>, meets in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palais_du_Luxembourg" title="Palais du Luxembourg" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBKA">Palais du Luxembourg</a>. The more important lower house, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Assembly_(France)" title="National Assembly (France)" id="mwBKE">National Assembly</a>, meets in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palais_Bourbon" title="Palais Bourbon" id="mwBKI">Palais Bourbon</a>. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_presidents_of_the_Senate_of_France" title="List of presidents of the Senate of France" id="mwBKM">President of the Senate</a>, the second-highest public official in France, with the President of the Republic being the sole superior, resides in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petit_Luxembourg" title="Petit Luxembourg" id="mwBKQ">Petit Luxembourg</a>, a smaller palace annexe to the Palais du Luxembourg.<sup about="#mwt516" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-127" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-127"}}'><a href="#cite_note-127" id="mwBKU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBKY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKc">[</span>124<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBKk"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Conseil_d'Etat_Paris_WA.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBKo"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Conseil_d'Etat_Paris_WA.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Conseil_d%27Etat_Paris_WA.jpg/250px-Conseil_d%27Etat_Paris_WA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Conseil_d%27Etat_Paris_WA.jpg/500px-Conseil_d%27Etat_Paris_WA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2900" data-file-height="1000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="86" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBKs"/></a><figcaption id="mwBKw">The Palais-Royal, residence of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conseil_d'État_(France)" title="Conseil d'État (France)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBK0">Conseil d'État</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwBK4">France's highest courts are located in Paris. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Court_of_Cassation_(France)" title="Court of Cassation (France)" id="mwBK8">Court of Cassation</a>, the highest court in the judicial order, which reviews criminal and civil cases, is located in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palais_de_Justice,_Paris" title="Palais de Justice, Paris" id="mwBLA">Palais de Justice</a> on the <i id="mwBLE">Île de la Cité</i>.<sup about="#mwt519" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-128" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-128"}}'><a href="#cite_note-128" id="mwBLI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLQ">[</span>125<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLU">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_of_State_(France)" title="Council of State (France)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBLY">Conseil d'État</a>, which provides legal advice to the executive and acts as the highest court in the administrative order, judging litigation against public bodies, is located in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palais-Royal" title="Palais-Royal" id="mwBLc">Palais-Royal</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1st_arrondissement_of_Paris" title="1st arrondissement of Paris" id="mwBLg">1st arrondissement</a>.<sup about="#mwt522" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-129" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-129"}}'><a href="#cite_note-129" id="mwBLk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLs">[</span>126<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLw">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitutional_Council_of_France" title="Constitutional Council of France" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBL0">Constitutional Council</a>, an advisory body with ultimate authority on the constitutionality of laws and government decrees, meets in the Montpensier wing of the Palais Royal.<sup about="#mwt525" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-130" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-130"}}'><a href="#cite_note-130" id="mwBL4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBL8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMA">[</span>127<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBME">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBMI">Paris and its region host the headquarters of several international organisations, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNESCO" title="UNESCO" id="mwBMM">UNESCO</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organisation_for_Economic_Co-operation_and_Development" title="Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBMQ">Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Chamber_of_Commerce" title="International Chamber of Commerce" id="mwBMU">International Chamber of Commerce</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Club" title="Paris Club" id="mwBMY">Paris Club</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Space_Agency" title="European Space Agency" id="mwBMc">European Space Agency</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Energy_Agency" title="International Energy Agency" id="mwBMg">International Energy Agency</a>, the <i id="mwBMk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organisation_internationale_de_la_Francophonie" title="Organisation internationale de la Francophonie" id="mwBMo">Organisation internationale de la Francophonie</a></i>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Union_Institute_for_Security_Studies" title="European Union Institute for Security Studies" id="mwBMs">European Union Institute for Security Studies</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Bureau_of_Weights_and_Measures" title="International Bureau of Weights and Measures" id="mwBMw">International Bureau of Weights and Measures</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bureau_of_International_Expositions" title="Bureau of International Expositions" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBM0">International Exhibition Bureau</a>, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Federation_for_Human_Rights" title="International Federation for Human Rights" id="mwBM4">International Federation for Human Rights</a>.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwBM8" aria-labelledby="Police_force"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Police_force">Police force</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBNA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Gendarmerie_BMW_R1100RT.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBNE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Gendarmerie_BMW_R1100RT.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Gendarmerie_BMW_R1100RT.jpg/250px-Gendarmerie_BMW_R1100RT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Gendarmerie_BMW_R1100RT.jpg/500px-Gendarmerie_BMW_R1100RT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3072" data-file-height="2048" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBNI"/></a><figcaption id="mwBNM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Gendarmerie" title="National Gendarmerie" id="mwBNQ">Gendarmerie</a> motorcyclists</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBNU">The security of Paris is mainly the responsibility of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prefecture_of_Police_of_Paris" title="Prefecture of Police of Paris" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBNY">Prefecture of Police of Paris</a>, a subdivision of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minister_of_the_Interior_(France)" title="Minister of the Interior (France)" id="mwBNc">Ministry of the Interior</a>. It supervises the units of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Police_(France)" title="National Police (France)" id="mwBNg">National Police</a> who patrol the city and the three neighbouring departments. It is also responsible for providing emergency services, including the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Fire_Brigade" title="Paris Fire Brigade" id="mwBNk">Paris Fire Brigade</a>. Its headquarters is on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Place_Louis_Lépine" title="Place Louis Lépine" id="mwBNo">Place Louis Lépine</a> on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île_de_la_Cité" title="Île de la Cité" id="mwBNs">Île de la Cité</a>.<sup about="#mwt528" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Presentation_Generale_131-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Presentation Generale"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Presentation_Generale-131"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Presentation_Generale-131" id="mwBNw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBN0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBN4">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBN8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBOA">There are 43,800 officers under the prefecture, and a fleet of more than 6,000 vehicles, including police cars, motorcycles, fire trucks, boats, and helicopters.<sup about="#mwt529" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Presentation_Generale_131-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Presentation Generale"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Presentation_Generale-131" id="mwBOE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBOI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOM">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The national police has its own special unit for riot control and crowd control, and security of public buildings, called the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compagnies_Républicaines_de_Sécurité" title="Compagnies Républicaines de Sécurité" id="mwBOU">Compagnies Républicaines de Sécurité</a> (CRS). Vans of CRS agents are frequently seen in the centre of Paris when there are demonstrations and public events. The police are supported by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Gendarmerie" title="National Gendarmerie" id="mwBOY">National Gendarmerie</a>, a branch of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Armed_Forces" title="French Armed Forces" id="mwBOc">French Armed Forces</a>. Their police operations are supervised by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interior_ministry" title="Interior ministry" id="mwBOg">Ministry of the Interior</a>.<sup about="#mwt532" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-132" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-132"}}'><a href="#cite_note-132" id="mwBOk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBOo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOs">[</span>129<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBO0">Crime in Paris is similar to that in most large cities. Violent crime is relatively rare in the city centre. Political violence is uncommon, though very large demonstrations may occur in Paris and other French cities simultaneously. These demonstrations, usually managed by a strong police presence, can turn confrontational and escalate into violence.<sup about="#mwt535" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-133" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-133"}}'><a href="#cite_note-133" id="mwBO4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBO8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPA">[</span>130<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwBPI" aria-labelledby="Cityscape"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Cityscape">Cityscape</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt536" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBPM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"wide image","href":"./Template:Wide_image"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Tour Eiffel 360 Panorama.jpg"},"2":{"wt":"1600px"},"align-cap":{"wt":"center"},"3":{"wt":"A panorama of Paris from the Eiffel Tower, in a 360-degree view. The [[Seine]] river flows from the north-east to the south-west, right to left"},"dir":{"wt":"rtl"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1330227556" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt537" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Wide image/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .wide-image-normbg,.mw-parser-output .thumbimage.wide-image-normbg{background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle,#f8f9fa);color:inherit}.mw-parser-output .wide-image-nobg,.mw-parser-output .thumbimage.wide-image-nobg{background:transparent;color:inherit}</style></span><div class="thumb tnone" style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;overflow:hidden;width:auto;max-width:1610px" about="#mwt536" id="mwBPQ"><div class="thumbinner"><div class="noresize thumbimage" style="overflow:auto;direction:rtl"><span typeof="mw:File" data-mw='{"caption":"&lt;span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwBPU\">‪&lt;/span>A panorama of Paris from the Eiffel Tower, in a 360-degree view. The &lt;a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Seine\" title=\"Seine\" id=\"mwBPY\">Seine&lt;/a> river flows from the north-east to the south-west, right to left&lt;span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwBPc\">‬&lt;/span>"}'><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tour_Eiffel_360_Panorama.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="‪A panorama of Paris from the Eiffel Tower, in a 360-degree view. The Seine river flows from the north-east to the south-west, right to left‬"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tour_Eiffel_360_Panorama.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Tour_Eiffel_360_Panorama.jpg/1920px-Tour_Eiffel_360_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Tour_Eiffel_360_Panorama.jpg/3840px-Tour_Eiffel_360_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="10500" data-file-height="1400" data-file-type="bitmap" height="213" width="1600" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption" style="text-align:center"><div class="magnify"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tour_Eiffel_360_Panorama.jpg" title="File:Tour Eiffel 360 Panorama.jpg"> </a></div>A panorama of Paris from the Eiffel Tower, in a 360-degree view. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine" title="Seine">Seine</a> river flows from the north-east to the south-west, right to left</div></div></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="16" id="mwBPg" aria-labelledby="Urbanism_and_architecture"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Urbanism_and_architecture">Urbanism and architecture</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt538" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBPk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Architecture of Paris"},"2":{"wt":"Haussmann&apos;s renovation of Paris"},"3":{"wt":"Religious buildings in Paris"},"4":{"wt":"List of tallest buildings in the Paris region"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt539" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt538" id="mwBPo">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Architecture_of_Paris" title="Architecture of Paris">Architecture of Paris</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haussmann's_renovation_of_Paris" title="Haussmann's renovation of Paris">Haussmann's renovation of Paris</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Religious_buildings_in_Paris" title="Religious buildings in Paris">Religious buildings in Paris</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tallest_buildings_in_the_Paris_region" title="List of tallest buildings in the Paris region">List of tallest buildings in the Paris region</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBPs"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rue_de_Rivoli_at_night,_Paris_August_2013.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBPw"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rue_de_Rivoli_at_night,_Paris_August_2013.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Rue_de_Rivoli_at_night%2C_Paris_August_2013.jpg/250px-Rue_de_Rivoli_at_night%2C_Paris_August_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Rue_de_Rivoli_at_night%2C_Paris_August_2013.jpg/500px-Rue_de_Rivoli_at_night%2C_Paris_August_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4048" data-file-height="2880" data-file-type="bitmap" height="178" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBP0"/></a><figcaption id="mwBP4">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rue_de_Rivoli" title="Rue de Rivoli" id="mwBP8">Rue de Rivoli</a></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBQA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_Place_des_Vosges_02.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBQE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_Place_des_Vosges_02.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Paris_Place_des_Vosges_02.jpg/250px-Paris_Place_des_Vosges_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Paris_Place_des_Vosges_02.jpg/500px-Paris_Place_des_Vosges_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4515" data-file-height="3013" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBQI"/></a><figcaption id="mwBQM">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Place_des_Vosges" title="Place des Vosges" id="mwBQQ">Place des Vosges</a>, the oldest planned square in Paris</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBQU">Paris is one of the few world capitals that has rarely seen destruction by catastrophe or war. As a result, even its earliest history is visible in its street map, and centuries of rulers adding their respective architectural marks on the capital have resulted in an accumulated wealth of history-rich monuments and buildings whose beauty plays a large part in giving Paris the reputation it has today.<sup about="#mwt542" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-134" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-134"}}'><a href="#cite_note-134" id="mwBQY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBQc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQg">[</span>131<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQk">]</span></span></a></sup> At its origin, before the Middle Ages, Paris was composed of several islands and sandbanks in a bend of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine" title="Seine" id="mwBQo">Seine</a>. Of those, two remain today: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île_Saint-Louis" title="Île Saint-Louis" id="mwBQs">Île Saint-Louis</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île_de_la_Cité" title="Île de la Cité" id="mwBQw">Île de la Cité</a>. A third one is the 1827 artificially created <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île_aux_Cygnes" title="Île aux Cygnes" id="mwBQ0">Île aux Cygnes</a>.</p>

<p id="mwBQ4">Modern Paris owes much of its downtown plan and architectural harmony to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleon_III" title="Napoleon III" id="mwBQ8">Napoleon III</a> and his Prefect of the Seine, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georges-Eugène_Haussmann" title="Georges-Eugène Haussmann" id="mwBRA">Baron Haussmann</a>. Between <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haussmann's_renovation_of_Paris" title="Haussmann's renovation of Paris" id="mwBRE">1853 and 1870 they rebuilt the city centre</a>, created the wide downtown boulevards and squares where the boulevards intersected, imposed standard facades along the boulevards, and required that the facades be built of the distinctive cream-grey "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_stone" title="Paris stone" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBRI">Paris stone</a>". They built the major parks around central Paris.<sup about="#mwt548" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-135" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-135"}}'><a href="#cite_note-135" id="mwBRM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBRQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRU">[</span>132<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRY">]</span></span></a></sup> The high residential population of the city centre makes Paris much different from most other major western cities.<sup about="#mwt543" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBraimohVlek200812_136-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBraimohVlek200812"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBraimohVlek200812-136"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Braimoh"},"2":{"wt":"Vlek"},"3":{"wt":"2008"},"p":{"wt":"12"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBraimohVlek200812-136" id="mwBRc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBRg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRk">[</span>133<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBRs">Paris's urbanism laws have been under strict control since the early 17th century,<sup about="#mwt552" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-plan_hauteurs_137-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"plan hauteurs"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-plan_hauteurs-137"}}'><a href="#cite_note-plan_hauteurs-137" id="mwBRw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBR0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBR4">[</span>134<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBR8">]</span></span></a></sup> particularly where street-front alignment, building height and building distribution is concerned.<sup about="#mwt553" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-plan_hauteurs_137-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"plan hauteurs"}}'><a href="#cite_note-plan_hauteurs-137" id="mwBSA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBSE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSI">[</span>134<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSM">]</span></span></a></sup> The <span about="#mwt549" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBSQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"210"},"2":{"wt":"m"}},"i":0}}]}'>210</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt549"> </span><span about="#mwt549">m (690</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt549"> </span><span about="#mwt549">ft)</span> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tour_Montparnasse" title="Tour Montparnasse" id="mwBSU">Tour Montparnasse</a> was both Paris's and France's tallest building from 1973 until 2011,<sup about="#mwt556" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-138" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-138"}}'><a href="#cite_note-138" id="mwBSY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBSc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSg">[</span>135<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSk">]</span></span></a></sup> when the record was taken by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Défense" title="La Défense" id="mwBSo">La Défense</a> district's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tour_First" title="Tour First" id="mwBSs">Tour First</a> in the commune of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Courbevoie" title="Courbevoie" id="mwBSw">Courbevoie</a>.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="17" id="mwBS0" aria-labelledby="Housing"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Housing">Housing</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBS4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Front_de_Seine_-_Paris_15.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBS8"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Front_de_Seine_-_Paris_15.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Front_de_Seine_-_Paris_15.jpg/250px-Front_de_Seine_-_Paris_15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Front_de_Seine_-_Paris_15.jpg/500px-Front_de_Seine_-_Paris_15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="6000" data-file-height="4000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBTA"/></a><figcaption id="mwBTE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_de_Seine" title="Front de Seine" id="mwBTI">Front de Seine</a> development along the river <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine" title="Seine" id="mwBTM">Seine</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwBTQ">In 2018, the most expensive residential street in Paris by average price per square metre was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avenue_Montaigne" title="Avenue Montaigne" id="mwBTU">Avenue Montaigne</a>, at 22,372 euros per square metre.<sup about="#mwt560" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-139" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-139"}}'><a href="#cite_note-139" id="mwBTY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBTc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTg">[</span>136<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTk">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2011, the number of residences in the City of Paris was <span about="#mwt557" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBTo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"formatnum:1356074","function":"formatnum"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>1,356,074</span>. Among these, <span about="#mwt558" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBTs" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"formatnum:1165541","function":"formatnum"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>1,165,541</span> (85.9 percent) were main residences, <span about="#mwt559" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBTw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"formatnum:91835","function":"formatnum"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>91,835</span> (6.8 percent) were secondary residences, and the remaining 7.3 percent were empty.<sup about="#mwt563" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-insee_logement_140-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"insee_logement"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-insee_logement-140"}}'><a href="#cite_note-insee_logement-140" id="mwBT0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBT4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBT8">[</span>137<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBUE">Sixty-two percent of buildings date from 1949 and before, with 20 percent built between 1949 and 1974. 18 percent of Paris buildings were built after 1974.<sup about="#mwt566" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-notaires_idf_141-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"notaires_idf"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-notaires_idf-141"}}'><a href="#cite_note-notaires_idf-141" id="mwBUI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUQ">[</span>138<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUU">]</span></span></a></sup> Two-thirds of the city's 1.3 million residences are studio and two-room apartments. Paris averages 1.9 people per residence, a number that has remained constant since the 1980s, which is less than Île-de-France's 2.33 people-per-residence average. Only 33 percent of Parisian principal residents own their habitation, against 47 percent for the wider <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île-de-France" title="Île-de-France" id="mwBUY">Île-de-France</a> region. Most of Paris's population rents their residence.<sup about="#mwt567" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-notaires_idf_141-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"notaires_idf"}}'><a href="#cite_note-notaires_idf-141" id="mwBUc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUk">[</span>138<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUo">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2017, social or public housing was 19.9 percent of Paris's residences. Its distribution varies widely throughout Paris, from 2.6 percent of the housing in the wealthy 7th arrondissement to 39.9 percent in the 19th arrondissement.<sup about="#mwt568" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-142" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-142"}}'><a href="#cite_note-142" id="mwBUs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBU0">[</span>139<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBU4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBU8">In February 2019, a Paris NGO conducted its annual citywide count of homeless persons. They counted 3,641 homeless persons in Paris, of whom twelve percent were women. More than half had been homeless for more than a year. 2,885 were living in the streets or parks, 298 in train and metro stations, and 756 in other forms of temporary shelter. This was an increase of 588 persons since 2018.<sup about="#mwt569" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-143" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-143"}}'><a href="#cite_note-143" id="mwBVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBVE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVI">[</span>140<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="18" id="mwBVQ" aria-labelledby="Suburbs"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Suburbs">Suburbs</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBVU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris,_France,_September_24,_2016_SkySat.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBVY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris,_France,_September_24,_2016_SkySat.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Paris%2C_France%2C_September_24%2C_2016_SkySat.jpg/250px-Paris%2C_France%2C_September_24%2C_2016_SkySat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Paris%2C_France%2C_September_24%2C_2016_SkySat.jpg/500px-Paris%2C_France%2C_September_24%2C_2016_SkySat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2560" data-file-height="1120" data-file-type="bitmap" height="109" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBVc"/></a><figcaption id="mwBVg">Western Paris in 2016, photographed by a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SkySat" title="SkySat" id="mwBVk">SkySat</a> satellite</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBVo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:West_of_Paris_seen_from_Tour_Montparnasse_-_2019-09-18.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBVs"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:West_of_Paris_seen_from_Tour_Montparnasse_-_2019-09-18.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/West_of_Paris_seen_from_Tour_Montparnasse_-_2019-09-18.jpg/250px-West_of_Paris_seen_from_Tour_Montparnasse_-_2019-09-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/West_of_Paris_seen_from_Tour_Montparnasse_-_2019-09-18.jpg/500px-West_of_Paris_seen_from_Tour_Montparnasse_-_2019-09-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBVw"/></a><figcaption id="mwBV0">West of Paris seen from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tour_Montparnasse" title="Tour Montparnasse" id="mwBV4">Tour Montparnasse</a>, 2019</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBV8">Aside from the 20th-century addition of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bois_de_Boulogne" title="Bois de Boulogne" id="mwBWA">Bois de Boulogne</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bois_de_Vincennes" title="Bois de Vincennes" id="mwBWE">Bois de Vincennes</a>, and the Paris heliport, Paris's administrative limits have remained unchanged since 1860. A greater administrative <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine_(department)" title="Seine (department)" id="mwBWI">Seine</a> department had been governing Paris and its suburbs since its creation in 1790, but the rising suburban population had made it difficult to maintain as a unique entity. To address this problem, the parent "District de la région parisienne" ('district of the Paris region') was reorganised into several new departments from 1968: Paris became a department in itself, and the administration of its suburbs was divided between the three new departments surrounding it. The district of the Paris region was renamed "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île-de-France" title="Île-de-France" id="mwBWM">Île-de-France</a>" in 1977, but this abbreviated "Paris region" name is still commonly used today to describe the Île-de-France, and as a vague reference to the entire Paris agglomeration.<sup about="#mwt572" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-144" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-144"}}'><a href="#cite_note-144" id="mwBWQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBWU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBWY">[</span>141<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBWc">]</span></span></a></sup> Long-intended measures to unite Paris with its suburbs began in January 2016, when the Métropole du <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Paris" title="Grand Paris" id="mwBWg">Grand Paris</a> came into existence.<sup about="#mwt575" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MGP_118-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"MGP"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-MGP-118"}}'><a href="#cite_note-MGP-118" id="mwBWk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBWo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBWs">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBWw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBW0">Paris's disconnect with its suburbs, its lack of suburban transportation, in particular, became all too apparent with the Paris agglomeration's growth. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Delouvrier" title="Paul Delouvrier" id="mwBW4">Paul Delouvrier</a> promised to resolve the Paris-suburbs <i id="mwBW8">mésentente</i> when he became head of the Paris region in 1961.<sup about="#mwt576" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMasson1984536_145-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEMasson1984536"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMasson1984536-145"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Masson"},"2":{"wt":"1984"},"p":{"wt":"536"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMasson1984536-145" id="mwBXA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBXE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXI">[</span>142<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXM">]</span></span></a></sup> Two of his most ambitious projects for the Region were the construction of five suburban "villes nouvelles" ("new cities")<sup about="#mwt579" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEYarri2008407_146-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEYarri2008407"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEYarri2008407-146"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Yarri"},"2":{"wt":"2008"},"p":{"wt":"407"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEYarri2008407-146" id="mwBXQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBXU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXY">[</span>143<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXc">]</span></span></a></sup> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Réseau_Express_Régional" title="Réseau Express Régional" id="mwBXg">RER</a> commuter train network.<sup about="#mwt582" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGordon200646–47_147-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEGordon200646–47"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGordon200646–47-147"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Gordon"},"2":{"wt":"2006"},"pp":{"wt":"46–47"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGordon200646–47-147" id="mwBXk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBXo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXs">[</span>144<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBX0">Many other suburban residential districts (<i id="mwBX4">grands ensembles</i>) were built between the 1960s and 1970s to provide a low-cost solution for a rapidly expanding population.<sup about="#mwt585" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTECastells198375_148-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTECastells198375"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECastells198375-148"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Castells"},"2":{"wt":"1983"},"p":{"wt":"75"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTECastells198375-148" id="mwBX8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBYA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYE">[</span>145<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYI">]</span></span></a></sup> These districts were socially mixed at first,<sup about="#mwt588" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTETomasBlancBonillaIERP2003237_149-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTETomasBlancBonillaIERP2003237"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTETomasBlancBonillaIERP2003237-149"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Tomas"},"2":{"wt":"Blanc"},"3":{"wt":"Bonilla"},"4":{"wt":"IERP"},"5":{"wt":"2003"},"p":{"wt":"237"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTETomasBlancBonillaIERP2003237-149" id="mwBYM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBYQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYU">[</span>146<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYY">]</span></span></a></sup> but few residents actually owned their homes. The growing economy made these accessible to the middle classes only from the 1970s.<sup about="#mwt593" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-villes_nouvelles_150-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"villes nouvelles"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-villes_nouvelles-150"}}'><a href="#cite_note-villes_nouvelles-150" id="mwBYc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBYg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYk">[</span>147<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYo">]</span></span></a></sup> Their poor construction quality and their haphazard insertion into existing urban growth contributed to their desertion by those able to move elsewhere, and their repopulation by those with more limited resources.<sup about="#mwt594" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-villes_nouvelles_150-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"villes nouvelles"}}'><a href="#cite_note-villes_nouvelles-150" id="mwBYs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBYw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBY0">[</span>147<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBY4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBY8">These areas, <i id="mwBZA">quartiers sensibles</i> ("sensitive quarters"), are in northern and eastern Paris, namely around its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goutte_d'Or" title="Goutte d'Or" id="mwBZE">Goutte d'Or</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belleville,_Paris" title="Belleville, Paris" id="mwBZI">Belleville</a> neighbourhoods. To the north of Paris, they are grouped mainly in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine-Saint-Denis" title="Seine-Saint-Denis" id="mwBZM">Seine-Saint-Denis</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_(France)" title="Department (France)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBZQ">department</a>, and to a lesser extent, to the east in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Val-d'Oise" title="Val-d'Oise" id="mwBZU">Val-d'Oise</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_(France)" title="Department (France)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBZY">department</a>. Other difficult areas are located in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine" title="Seine" id="mwBZc">Seine</a> valley, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Évry_(Essonne)" title="Évry (Essonne)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBZg">Évry</a> et <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corbeil-Essonnes" title="Corbeil-Essonnes" id="mwBZk">Corbeil-Essonnes</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Essonne_(département)" title="Essonne (département)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBZo">Essonne</a>), in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Mureaux" title="Les Mureaux" id="mwBZs">Mureaux</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantes-la-Jolie" title="Mantes-la-Jolie" id="mwBZw">Mantes-la-Jolie</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yvelines" title="Yvelines" id="mwBZ0">Yvelines</a>), and scattered among social housing districts created by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Delouvrier" title="Paul Delouvrier" id="mwBZ4">Delouvrier</a>'s 1961 "ville nouvelle" political initiative.<sup about="#mwt597" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-151" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-151"}}'><a href="#cite_note-151" id="mwBZ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBaA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBaE">[</span>148<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBaI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBaM">The Paris agglomeration's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_sociology" title="Urban sociology" id="mwBaQ">urban sociology</a> is basically that of 19th-century Paris: the wealthy live in the west and southwest, and the middle-to-working classes are in the north and east. The remaining areas are mostly middle-class, dotted with wealthy islands in areas of historical importance, namely <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint-Maur-des-Fossés" title="Saint-Maur-des-Fossés" id="mwBaU">Saint-Maur-des-Fossés</a> to the east and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enghien-les-Bains" title="Enghien-les-Bains" id="mwBaY">Enghien-les-Bains</a> to the north of Paris.<sup about="#mwt600" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-152" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-152"}}'><a href="#cite_note-152" id="mwBac"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBak">[</span>149<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBao">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="19" id="mwBas" aria-labelledby="Demographics"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Demographics">Demographics</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt601" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBaw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Demographics of Paris"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt602" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt601" id="mwBa0">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demographics_of_Paris" title="Demographics of Paris">Demographics of Paris</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBa4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_population_pyramid.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBa8"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_population_pyramid.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Paris_population_pyramid.svg/250px-Paris_population_pyramid.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Paris_population_pyramid.svg/500px-Paris_population_pyramid.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2624" data-file-height="2104" data-file-type="drawing" height="200" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBbA"/></a><figcaption id="mwBbE">City of Paris population pyramid in 2022</figcaption></figure>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt603" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBbI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Collapsible Table Paris Region top countries &amp; territories of birth","href":"./Template:Collapsible_Table_Paris_Region_top_countries_&amp;_territories_of_birth"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234" about="#mwt604" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Infobox/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><table class="infobox" about="#mwt603" id="mwBbM"><tbody><tr><th colspan="2" class="infobox-above">2023 Census Paris Region</th></tr><tr><td colspan="2" class="infobox-subheader" style="font-weight:bold;">(<span title="French-language text"><i lang="fr"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Île-de-France" title="Île-de-France">Île-de-France</a></i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/>)<sup about="#mwt607" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-immig_153-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"immig"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-immig-153"}}'><a href="#cite_note-immig-153" id="mwBbQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBbU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbY">[</span>150<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt612" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-154" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-154"}}'><a href="#cite_note-154" id="mwBbg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBbk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbo">[</span>151<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbs">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" class="infobox-full-data"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border-spacing:0px 0px;border:none"><tbody><tr style="vertical-align:top"><th scope="col" style="text-align:left;"> Country/territory<br/>of birth</th><th scope="col" style="text-align:right;"> Population</th></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="background:#eee;text-align:left;"> <span class="flagicon"><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/France" title="France"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c3/Flag_of_France.svg/40px-Flag_of_France.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c3/Flag_of_France.svg/60px-Flag_of_France.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="France" data-file-width="900" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></span> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metropolitan_France" title="Metropolitan France">Metropolitan France</a></td><td style="background:#eee;text-align:right;"> 9,100,643</td></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="text-align:left;"> <span class="flagicon"><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algeria" title="Algeria"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Algeria.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Flag_of_Algeria.svg/40px-Flag_of_Algeria.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Flag_of_Algeria.svg/60px-Flag_of_Algeria.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Algeria" data-file-width="900" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></span> <a re